tablished","commission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":44,"blurb":"Listed by HotelGuides at \"1347 Center Street, Bowling Green, KY 42103\", \"24 miles from Mammoth Cave National Park\". Hyatt''s own page was not fetched (brand pages return 403), so nothing else about the property is stated here."},{"name":"Grand Victorian Inn","source":"https://visitparkcityky.com/stay","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["romance","culture","rail"],"booking_route":"own website grandvictorianinnky.com or phone 270-590-1935","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":45,"blurb":"5 Old Dixie Hwy, Park City (\"formerly the Mentz Hotel\"): \"thirteen unique rooms\" in \"an historic 1885 Mammoth Cave Victorian train station hotel\", with the Mammoth Railway Cafe event venue; free breakfast; adults only; no pets; 270-590-1935."},{"name":"Miss Betty''s Diner","source":"https://visitparkcityky.com/eat","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in; phone 270-544-7616","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":46,"blurb":"24130 Louisville Road (31W), Park City: \"Home Style food with southern favorites such as delicious Southern Fried Catfish, Manhattan, Meatloaf, Slow-smoked BBQ, Chicken and Dumplings\", homemade soups and fresh pies; 270-544-7616."},{"name":"Esters Farm Cafe","source":"https://visitparkcityky.com/eat","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in; phone 270-544-7341","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":47,"blurb":"4900 Park City Bon Ayr Road, Park City: \"scratch-made comfort food in a charming space that feels like home. Specialties include brown butter pork chops, pot roast, savory tomato pie\"; 270-544-7341."},{"name":"Blue Holler Cafe","source":"https://www.cavesandlakes.com/things-to-do/dining/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","culture"],"booking_route":"walk-in (Facebook page only; hours not read)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":48,"blurb":"Edmonson County: \"Serving Authentic German Cuisine and Classic American Fare. The location is cozy, country, and quirky; the cuisine is unique, bold, and undeniably memorable. Open seasonally.\""},{"name":"Porky Pig Diner","source":"https://www.cavesandlakes.com/things-to-do/dining/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in (Facebook page only; hours not read)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":49,"blurb":"Edmonson County: \"A family-run country diner that serves up homestyle cooking with all the southern favorites. Don''t miss the Sunday buffet!\""},{"name":"Tre Pizza","source":"https://www.cavesandlakes.com/things-to-do/dining/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in (Facebook page only; hours not read)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":50,"blurb":"Edmonson County: \"Authentic Italian-style pizza, dough imported from Italy, locally-sourced ingredients, smoked wings, specialty sandwiches, dessert pies, and beer to dine-in customers.\""},{"name":"Kristin''s Kitchen","source":"https://www.cavesandlakes.com/things-to-do/dining/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary"],"booking_route":"dine-in or carry-out","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":51,"blurb":"Edmonson County: \"Fresh, homemade food for dine-in or carry-out; specialize in catering and charcuterie boards.\" Own site kristinskitchenky.com (not fetched)."},{"name":"Warnell Family Pharmacy & Soda Shoppe","source":"https://www.cavesandlakes.com/things-to-do/dining/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","culinary"],"booking_route":"walk-in","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":52,"blurb":"Edmonson County: \"Nostalgia with a twist! A modern, yet charming, joint pharmacy/soda shoppe serving the classics - malts, sweets, sandwiches, soup\"."},{"name":"Park City","source":"https://visitparkcityky.com/eat","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","motoring"],"booking_route":"none needed - a town","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":53,"blurb":"The I-65 Exit 48 gateway - \"I-65 Exit 48 DIRECT ACCESS to Mammoth cave national park\" (Park City Tourism) - and the southern trailhead of the 9-mile railroad bike trail; diners, the Grand Victorian Inn and cottages; Family Dollar and Dollar General at the exit \"Great for picnickers, hikers, bikers, paddlers, campers and RV enthusiasts\"."},{"name":"Cave City","source":"https://cavecity.com/lodging/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","motoring"],"booking_route":"none needed - a town","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":54,"blurb":"The I-65 Exit 53 gateway on the NPS''s north-approach directions; Cave City Tourism: \"Between our hotel rooms, cabins, teepees, RV parks, and camping, visitors can find the perfect accommodations\"; welcome centre at 821 Mammoth Cave St, (270) 773-8833."},{"name":"Brownsville","source":"https://www.cavesandlakes.com/things-to-do/dining/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","adventure"],"booking_route":"none needed - a town","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":55,"blurb":"The Edmonson County seat on the park''s west side: Houchin Ferry Campground is \"one and a half miles from the town of Brownsville\" (NPS); the county tourism commission lists diners, a soda shoppe and Nolin Lake''s Lakeside Cafe; PO Box 628 Brownsville, 270-597-2222."}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Mammoth Cave National Park free?","a":"Entry is: \"There is no fee to enter Mammoth Cave National Park. However, there are fees associated with cave tours, camping, and shelter rentals.\" Tours run from $15 (Mammoth Passage, adult) to $79 (Wild Cave).","source":"https://www.nps.gov/maca/planyourvisit/fees.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Do you need reservations for Mammoth Cave National Park?","a":"Not to enter, but to go into the cave: \"Tickets are required to enter Mammoth Cave. Reservations are strongly recommended. Reservations are the only way to ensure a spot is available for your party.\" Book on Recreation.gov or at 877-444-6777; \"Availability of walk-up tickets is not guaranteed.\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/maca/faqs.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"What should I wear to Mammoth Cave?","a":"The NPS says cave temperatures \"usually hover around 54°F (12.2°C), year-round. A light jacket or sweater is recommended, as are good shoes for walking.\" The crawling tours require \"lace-up hiking boots that cover the ankle\" with slip-resistant tread.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/maca/faqs.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you camp at Mammoth Cave National Park?","a":"Yes. \"Mammoth Cave National Park has three frontcountry campgrounds\" - Mammoth Cave, Maple Springs and Houchin Ferry - plus backcountry and riverside sites. \"All camping in the park requires a permit and most sites are available by reservation\" on Recreation.gov.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/maca/planyourvisit/camping.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you kayak in Mammoth Cave National Park?","a":"Yes: \"Over 30 miles of the Green and Nolin Rivers trace through the Mammoth Cave National Park\". The popular Dennison Ferry to Green River Ferry trip is 7.6 miles, 2.5 to 4 hours. Children 12 and under must wear a life jacket, and river use is prohibited at or above 20 feet on the park gauge.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/maca/planyourvisit/canoeing-kayaking-and-boating.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you bring dogs to Mammoth Cave National Park?","a":"On the surface, yes: \"Leashed pets are allowed on all surface trails in the park\" on a leash up to 6 feet, but \"Pets are not permitted in caves or park buildings.\" The Lodge runs a self-service day kennel; dogs need proof of rabies, DHLP, Bordetella and parvo vaccination.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/maca/planyourvisit/pets.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"What is the closest airport to Mammoth Cave National Park?","a":"\"The closest full-service international airports to the park are Louisville International Airport (80 minutes) and Nashville International Airport (90 minutes).\" The directions page puts Louisville 89 miles and Nashville 99 miles from park headquarters, with car rentals at both.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/maca/faqs.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"How does the Green River Ferry at Mammoth Cave work?","a":"\"The Green River Ferry operates year-round with the exception of December 25\" and \"is free to use\". Hours are \"6 a.m. to 6 p.m. CST\"; vehicles must not exceed 12 tons or 16 feet, and service depends on river levels - call the hotline at (270) 758-2166.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/maca/planyourvisit/directions.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"What time zone is Mammoth Cave National Park in?","a":"\"Mammoth Cave is on Central Time (GMT-5). Visitors coming from the north will cross the boundary from the Eastern Time zone (GMT-4) at the northern Hart County line.\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/maca/faqs.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Is Mammoth Cave National Park wheelchair accessible?","a":"Partly. \"The Accessible Tour was expressly created for visitors with mobility devices such as motorized wheelchairs or walkers. There are no stairs on this tour\". The visitor center \"is fully accessible\", and \"The Heritage Trail, Echo River Spring Trail, Sand Cave Trail, and the Sloan''s Crossing Pond Trail are all wheelchair accessible.\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/maca/planyourvisit/accessibility.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Mammoth Cave National Park: Cave Tours, Green River & Where to Stay | TravelWell","meta_description":"Free entry to the world''s longest known cave system: ranger cave tours from $15, Green River paddling, three campgrounds, the Lodge and stays nearby.","slug":"mammoth-cave-national-park-kentucky","primary_keyword":"Mammoth Cave National Park","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination"},"hero":{"query":"Mammoth Cave National Park Historic Entrance"}}'::jsonb, 49),
