d","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":53,"blurb":"the NPS kit list for the valley: \"Not all trailheads have drinking water, so remember to bring water with you.\" \"Have a first aid kit in your bag.\" \"Use a trail map.\""},{"name":"Sturdy hiking shoes and waterproof boots","source":"https://www.nps.gov/cuva/planyourvisit/safety.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","family"],"booking_route":"retail referral (REI.com via AvantLink; Amazon Associates)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":3,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":54,"blurb":"\"Wear or bring sturdy hiking shoes when going on a trail.\" \"During wet conditions, wear waterproof boots with a heavy tread and step carefully.\" The Ledges trails are \"rocky, some steps\" (NPS hiking page)"},{"name":"Bug spray, sunscreen and light-coloured clothing","source":"https://www.nps.gov/cuva/planyourvisit/safety.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","family","senior"],"booking_route":"retail referral (Rab US and REI.com via AvantLink; Amazon Associates)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":3,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":55,"blurb":"\"Bring bug spray and sunscreen to protect your skin.\" \"Use repellents and follow label instructions.\" \"Wear light-colored clothing to easily find ticks.\""},{"name":"Sheraton Suites Akron Cuyahoga Falls","source":"https://www.visitakron-summit.org/listing/sheraton-suites-akron-cuyahoga-falls/220/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior"],"booking_route":"marriott.com (brand booking; not fetched - HTTP 403)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":8,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":56,"blurb":"listed by the Akron/Summit CVB in Cuyahoga Falls: \"On-site restaurant, TheLink@Sheraton, free high-speed internet, indoor pool, whirlpool, sauna, fitness center.\" Marriott''s own page refused the fetch (HTTP 403), so nothing else is stated here"},{"name":"Homewood Suites by Hilton Akron/Fairlawn","source":"https://www.visitakron-summit.org/listing/homewood-suites-by-hilton-akron-fairlawn/336/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior"],"booking_route":"hilton.com (brand booking; not fetched - HTTP 403)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":57,"blurb":"listed by the Akron/Summit CVB in Akron: \"All suites with full kitchens, high-speed internet, complimentary breakfast, free parking, swimming pool, fitness center and meeting room.\" Hilton''s own page refused the fetch (HTTP 403)"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Cuyahoga Valley National Park free?","a":"Yes. The NPS states: \"No, Cuyahoga Valley is a fee-free park that does not require a reservation for entry.\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/cuva/faqs.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Do you need a pass for Cuyahoga Valley National Park?","a":"No. \"An entrance pass is not required to access Cuyahoga Valley National Park.\" Two picnic shelters need reservations with fees.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/cuva/planyourvisit/fees.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"Can you camp in Cuyahoga Valley National Park?","a":"No. The NPS: \"No, Cuyahoga Valley National Park does not offer camping but you can discover camping nearby.\" Campgrounds outside the park range from Heritage Farms in Peninsula to state parks within 50 miles.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/cuva/faqs.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Where can you stay in Cuyahoga Valley National Park?","a":"The NPS names two lodging properties in the park: \"These are Stanford House and the Inn at Brandywine Falls\", and says nearby communities offer more.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/cuva/faqs.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you bring dogs to Cuyahoga Valley National Park?","a":"Yes, on a leash: \"Dogs can go on most of the trails in the park, but they must remain on a leash.\" Dogs are prohibited on the mountain bike trails.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/cuva/faqs.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you fish in Cuyahoga Valley National Park?","a":"Yes, with a state licence: the NPS says that if you have a valid Ohio fishing license then you can fish in the park.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/cuva/faqs.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Is there a train in Cuyahoga Valley National Park?","a":"Yes. The Cuyahoga Valley Scenic Railroad runs through the park, and in season the NPS says you can \"bike or hike the Towpath Trail or paddle the river in one direction, and ride the train back\". The 2026 Explorer program ran June 1 to September 7.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/cuva/planyourvisit/train.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Cuyahoga Valley National Park?","a":"For fall colour, the NPS says \"Peak color is usually during the third week of October\" - Oak Hill early in the month, Brandywine Falls mid-month and the Ledges late - and advises weekdays or morning and late afternoon to avoid crowded lots.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/thingstodo/best-fall-colors-cuyahoga-valley.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"Is Cuyahoga Valley National Park closed?","a":"The park is open, with dated closures: the Towpath from Boston Trailhead to Lock 29 in Peninsula, \"Tentative closure dates: August 24–November 20, 2026 and March 29–April 21, 2027\"; a \"River-wide closure near river mile 17 due to bridge construction\"; part of Oak Hill Road; and Dickerson Run Trail, \"closed until further notice.\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/cuva/planyourvisit/conditions.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"What should you wear to Cuyahoga Valley National Park?","a":"The NPS says: \"Wear or bring sturdy hiking shoes when going on a trail\"; \"During wet conditions, wear waterproof boots with a heavy tread\"; and \"Wear light-colored clothing to easily find ticks.\" It also says to bring water, bug spray and sunscreen.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/cuva/planyourvisit/safety.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Cuyahoga Valley National Park: Towpath, Scenic Railroad & Brandywine Falls | TravelWell","meta_description":"A free national park between Cleveland and Akron: the Towpath and train, Brandywine Falls, current closures, and stays from an 1848 inn to Valley Overlook.","slug":"cuyahoga-valley-national-park-ohio","primary_keyword":"Cuyahoga Valley National Park","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination"},"hero":{"query":"Cuyahoga Valley National Park, Ohio"}}'::jsonb, 50)
