ght, Lake View Beach 1.5 miles north"},{"name":"West Beach 3-Loop Hike","source":"https://www.nps.gov/indu/planyourvisit/hiking.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["hiking","wildlife"],"booking_route":"no booking","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":7,"blurb":"moderate to rugged, 3.4 miles, about 2.5 hours, linking the dune, beach and Long Lake loops from West Beach"},{"name":"Century of Progress Homes, Lake Front Drive, Beverly Shores","source":"https://www.nps.gov/indu/planyourvisit/historical-sites.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["culture","senior"],"booking_route":"tours via the Indiana Dunes Visitor Center; Indiana Landmarks tour booking not observed","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":8,"blurb":"five homes from the 1933 Chicago World''s Fair - House of Tomorrow, Florida Tropical House, Armco-Ferro House, Cypress Log Cabin and Wieboldt-Rostone House - four rehabilitated through partnerships with Indiana Landmarks"},{"name":"Chellberg Farm and the Bailly Homestead","source":"https://www.nps.gov/indu/learn/historyculture/chellberg-farm.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["culture","family","senior"],"booking_route":"ranger tours via the NPS calendar and visitor center","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":9,"blurb":"a Swedish immigrant farm owned by the Chellbergs by 1874 - 1885 brick farmhouse, c.1872 barn, a 1930s sugar shack - beside the Bailly Homestead National Historic Landmark; the farmhouse opens \"during festivals, demonstrations, and ranger-guided tours\""},{"name":"Indiana Dunes Visitor Center, Porter","source":"https://www.nps.gov/indu/planyourvisit/idnlvc.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["family","culture"],"booking_route":"walk-in; 219-395-1882","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":10,"blurb":"shared by the national park and Indiana Dunes Tourism - exhibits on the dunes and state park, passes, passport stamps, orientation videos, artist exhibits and an Eastern National bookstore"},{"name":"Portage Lakefront and Riverwalk","source":"https://www.nps.gov/indu/planyourvisit/accessibility.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["senior","family","ocean"],"booking_route":"no booking","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":11,"blurb":"a beach with parking 0.125 miles from the water, \"A predominantly cement walkway\" and seasonal beach mats, at the park''s western end"},{"name":"Paul H. Douglas Trail and Center (Miller Woods)","source":"https://www.nps.gov/indu/planyourvisit/accessibility.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["senior","family","wildlife"],"booking_route":"equipment by phone, (219) 395-1821, free","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":12,"blurb":"a 3.4-mile trail through wetlands and rare black oak savanna; the center lends a Freedom Trax, a beach-capable Zoom Chair and a children''s trail chair free by reservation"},{"name":"Prairie Duneland and Calumet bike trails","source":"https://www.nps.gov/indu/planyourvisit/biking.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["family","sports","adventure"],"booking_route":"no booking","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":13,"blurb":"six NPS-listed bike trails including the paved 22.4-mile round-trip Prairie Duneland rail trail and the gravel 19.0-mile Calumet Trail; the paved Dunes Kankakee trail links to the state park"},{"name":"Maple Sugar Time Festival at Chellberg Farm (March)","source":"https://www.indianadunes.com/events/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["family","culture"],"booking_route":"not observed","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":14,"blurb":"the annual spring festival at the farm''s sugar shack, listed by the county tourism bureau; 2027 date not shown"},{"name":"Indiana Dunes Birding Festival (May)","source":"https://www.indianadunes.com/events/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["wildlife","senior","group"],"booking_route":"not observed","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":15,"blurb":"the region''s spring birding festival, listed by Indiana Dunes Tourism, in a park the bureau credits with 350 bird species"},{"name":"Kit the park asks for: sun protection and water","source":"https://www.nps.gov/indu/planyourvisit/safety.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","family","ocean"],"booking_route":"affiliate referral to a gear retailer (REI.com via AvantLink, or Amazon)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":3,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":16,"blurb":"The NPS: \"Wear sun protection. UVA/UVB sunscreen, a hat, lightweight and light-colored clothing, and sunglasses are recommended.\" and \"Drink plenty of water. Stay hydrated and drink before you feel thirsty.\""},{"name":"Kit the park asks for: tick and mosquito protection","source":"https://www.nps.gov/indu/planyourvisit/safety.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","wildlife","family"],"booking_route":"affiliate referral to a gear retailer (REI.com via AvantLink, or Amazon)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":3,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":17,"blurb":"The NPS: \"Wear light colored, long-sleeved shirts and tucked-in pants to help prevent both tick and mosquito bites.\" and \"Wear insect repellent containing permethrin, DEET or another EPS-approved repellent.\""},{"name":"Kit the park asks for: winter