0,"blurb":"check in at three of the trail''s pizzerias - among them Pizza Terra (Chesterton), Joe & Freddy''s and Cappo''s (Valparaiso) - on the Indiana Dunes Tourism app to earn a pub glass and sticker"},{"name":"Journeyman Distillery, The Featherbone Factory, Three Oaks, Michigan","source":"https://www.journeyman.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["culture","romance","group"],"booking_route":"OpenTable (restaurant); lodging route not observed","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat","activities"],"draw_rank":41,"blurb":"the original distillery at 109 Generations Drive with tours and tastings, Staymaker Restaurant, a putting green, event spaces and lodging"},{"name":"Lemon Creek Winery and farm market, Berrien Springs, Michigan","source":"https://www.lemoncreekwinery.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["wine","family","culinary"],"booking_route":"walk-in","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":42,"blurb":"\"locally owned and operated for more than 160 years\" at 533 E Lemon Creek Rd - estate-grown wines plus a seasonal farm market with pick-your-own fruit; open daily"},{"name":"Round Barn Winery, Brewery & Distillery, Baroda, Michigan","source":"https://www.roundbarn.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["wine","group","culinary"],"booking_route":"not observed","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":43,"blurb":"a combined winery, brewery and distillery in Southwest Michigan''s wine country (site behind an age gate; detail not observed)"},{"name":"Lake Michigan Shore Wine Trail","source":"https://miwinetrail.com/memberwineries","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["wine","romance","group"],"booking_route":"self-guided; interactive map on the trail site","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":44,"blurb":"14 member wineries in the Lake Michigan Shore AVA, a region holding 90% of Michigan''s vineyards where the lake extends the growing season - Domaine Berrien, Hickory Creek, Lemon Creek and White Pine among them"},{"name":"Valparaiso Popcorn Festival","source":"https://www.valparaisoevents.com/event/valparaiso-popcorn-festival","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["culinary","family","culture"],"booking_route":"walk-in, free street festival","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":45,"blurb":"47th year in 2026 (held September 12) with 340+ vendors downtown and \"the nation''s first Popcorn Parade\"; the 2027 date was not yet posted"},{"name":"Garwood Orchard & Farm Market, LaPorte","source":"http://garwoodapplefarm.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["family","culture"],"booking_route":"phone 219-362-4385; online shop via Mercato","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities","eat"],"draw_rank":46,"blurb":"u-pick apples and berries, a farm market bakery (cider, donuts, caramel apples) and horse and tractor wagon rides at 5911 W 50 South; u-pick daily September 4 to October 31"},{"name":"Broken Wagon Bison, Hobart","source":"https://www.brokenwagonbison.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["family","wildlife","group"],"booking_route":"phone only, 219-759-3523","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":47,"blurb":"guided bison ranch tours at 563 West 450 North - public tours Saturdays June to September at 11 and 2, private groups of 20+ June 1 to October 30; adults $15, ages 6-16 $10"},{"name":"Friendship Botanic Gardens, Michigan City","source":"https://friendshipbotanicgardens.org/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["wellness","senior","romance"],"booking_route":"gate admission; weddings and events by contact form or phone","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":48,"blurb":"100+ acres of landscaped and wooded gardens and trails, open Tuesday-Sunday 9-5 (Thursdays to 7 in June-August), $5 on Wednesdays, Thursday yoga May-September"},{"name":"Washington Park & Beach, Michigan City","source":"https://michigancitylaporte.com/see-and-do-category/recreation/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["family","ocean"],"booking_route":"no booking observed","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":49,"blurb":"the city''s Lake Michigan beach park, listed by the LaPorte County visitor bureau alongside the Bismarck Hill trail across 3 restored dunes"},{"name":"Foil MC, Michigan City","source":"https://foilmc.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["adventure","sports"],"booking_route":"booking buttons on own site; engine not identified","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities","gear"],"draw_rank":50,"blurb":"e-foil and wing-foil lessons and gear, \"100% mobile\" across Michigan City, New Buffalo, Chicago and surrounding lakes; ages 10 to 75"},{"name":"Stoke Riders, St. Joseph, Michigan","source":"https://stokeriders.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["adventure","sports"],"booking_route":"FareHarbor (lessons)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities","gear"],"draw_rank":51,"blurb":"kiteboarding, wing-foil and e-foil instruction, rentals and gear on the Michigan shore, with IKO-certified instruction and radio-coached lessons"},{"name":"Sunken Pelican Beach Rentals, Michigan City","source":"https://akstrelinski.wixsite.com/sunkenpelicanllc","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["family","ocean"],"booking_route":"Book Now on own Wix site; phone 219-214-3531 or email","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":52,"blurb":"a locally owned beach-equipment rental with free delivery across northwest Indiana and Michiana"},{"name":"Hot Tomolly Luxury Yacht Charters, Michigan City","source":"https://hottomolly.info/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["romance","group","ocean"],"booking_route":"phone/email only, (219) 763-3777","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":53,"blurb":"a fully crewed 76'' Lazzara motor yacht for sunset cruises, wine dinners, water sports and cross-lake trips to Chicago; site states rates begin at $2,500 but references a 2018 rate sheet"},{"name":"Michigan City charter fishing fleet","source":"https://michigancitylaporte.com/see-and-do-category/recreation/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["group","family","ocean"],"booking_route":"phone only per the bureau listing","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":54,"blurb":"Lake Michigan charters listed by the LaPorte County visitor bureau - Cloud Nine (a 32-foot Marinette), Crorkindill Charters and Just 1 More - out of a port the bureau places 35 nautical miles from downtown Chicago"}],"faq":[{"q":"What is the difference between Indiana Dunes National Park and the state park?","a":"They are two parks run by two agencies. The state park is run by the Indiana DNR and charges its own gate fee ($7 Indiana vehicles, $20 out-of-state per day); the NPS states national park passes do not apply at the state park.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/indu/planyourvisit/fees.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"What does it cost to enter Indiana Dunes National Park?","a":"A 7-day pass is $25 per private vehicle, $20 per motorcycle or $15 per person 16 and older; the park''s annual pass is $45. The America the Beautiful pass is $80 for residents and $250 for non-residents.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/indu/planyourvisit/fees.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"How do I get to Indiana Dunes National Park from Chicago?","a":"By train or car. The NPS states \"The Chicago and South Shore Train has stops within the park\"; the South Shore Line runs from Millennium Station in downtown Chicago, with Dune Park, Beverly Shores and Michigan City 11th St among its stations.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/indu/planyourvisit/directions.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"Can you camp at Indiana Dunes National Park?","a":"Yes, at Dunewood Campground in Beverly Shores: 67 sites (54 drive-in RV or tent, 13 tent-only), showers and a dump station, no electric or water hookups, open April 1 through November 1 at $25 a night, reserved on recreation.gov six months ahead.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/indu/planyourvisit/campgrounds.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"Can you rent a boat at Indiana Dunes National Park?","a":"Not in the park. The NPS states \"No marinas, boat rentals, or launches operate within the park itself\" and points to commercial facilities in Porter, Lake and LaPorte counties; hand-carried non-motorized boats may launch from park beaches except West Beach''s lifeguarded area in peak season.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/indu/planyourvisit/fishing-and-boating.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"Can you bring dogs to Indiana Dunes National Park?","a":"Yes, on a leash: \"Pets must be restrained on a leash no longer than 6 feet (2 meters).\" They are allowed on beaches year-round except the West Beach lifeguarded area from Memorial Day weekend to Labor Day weekend, and \"Pets are not allowed on the Pinhook Bog Trail\". Service animals may go everywhere.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/indu/planyourvisit/pets.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"What should I bring to Indiana Dunes?","a":"The NPS recommends \"UVA/UVB sunscreen, a hat, lightweight and light-colored clothing, and sunglasses\", plenty of water, long sleeves and tucked-in pants with insect repellent against ticks and mosquitoes, and in winter \"layers of loose-fitting clothes (including headwear)\".","source":"https://www.nps.gov/indu/planyourvisit/safety.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you swim at Indiana Dunes National Park?","a":"Yes. West Beach has lifeguards from the Friday of Memorial Day weekend through the Monday of Labor Day weekend, 10 am to 6 pm, and eight named beaches carry restrooms and potable water.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/indu/planyourvisit/swimming.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"What is the weather like at Indiana Dunes National Park?","a":"The NPS: \"Summers are warm and humid with high temperatures generally in the mid-80ºF''s (30ºC) and low temperatures in the mid-60ºF''s (18ºC)\"; \"Highs in winter are usually in the low to mid 30sºF (0ºC) with low temperatures in the low 20sºF (-5ºC)\". Lake Michigan weather \"can change quickly.\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/indu/planyourvisit/weather.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Indiana Dunes National Park: West Beach, Mount Baldy & the South Shore Line | TravelWell","meta_description":"Lake Michigan dunes by train from Chicago: West Beach, Mount Baldy ranger hikes, Dunewood camping, and the stays, food and gear around Porter and Michigan City.","slug":"indiana-dunes-national-park-indiana","primary_keyword":"Indiana Dunes National Park","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination"},"hero":{"query":"Indiana Dunes National Park, Indiana"}}'::jsonb, 51),
  ('voyageurs-minnesota', '12A', 'Voyageurs National Park', 'United States', 'Boat-in lake country and Kettle Falls', 'future', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'The Great Lakes', '{"adventure","wildlife","family","culture","parks"}', '{"remote","wild","serene","adventurous"}', '{}', null, null, '{"safety":{"posture":"book-freely","source":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/usa","verified":"2026-10-08"},"jewels":[{"name":"Kettle Falls Hotel","source":"https://www.kettlefallshotel.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culture","adventure","family"],"booking_route":"phone 218-240-1724 / 218-240-1726 or Kettlefalls@frontiernet.net; 30% deposit","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":1,"blurb":"The park''s only lodging, run by \"Official Concessioners of Voyageurs National Park\": hotel rooms (Double $110, Single $90 a night) and villas with a 3-night minimum (Non-Kitchen $210, Kitchen $260, Suite sleeping up to 8 $390); rents boats, canoes ($25/day) and kayaks ($35/day); shuttle \"$ 50.00/person round trip\". \"Tough place to get to..... But well worth it once you get there!\""},{"name":"Kettle Falls Cruise and Tour (ranger-led)","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/planyourvisit/guided-tours.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culture","family","senior"],"booking_route":"Recreation.gov \"VNP Boat Tours\" or 1-877-444-6777","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":2,"blurb":"From the Rainy Lake Visitor Center on the Voyageur, the \"Kettle Falls Cruise (6.5 hrs)\" is a \"Hotel visit with 2-hour ground tour plus dam exploration\"; from Kabetogama/Namakan on the Ne-Zho-Dain, the \"Kettle Falls Tour (5.5 hrs)\" with a 2-hour land tour. Season mid-June through the end of September; tickets from April 15 at 9am."},{"name":"Ellsworth Rock Gardens","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/learn/historyculture/ellsworth-rock-gardens.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culture","family","senior"],"booking_route":"none needed - free day-use site reached by boat; a 2.5-hour ranger tour runs on the Ne-Zho-Dain (Recreation.gov)","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":3,"blurb":"\"Showplace of Lake Kabetogama\" since the 1940s: Chicago carpenter Jack Ellsworth built \"62 terraced flower beds\" with \"more than 13,000 lilies\" and \"over 200 abstract rock sculptures that have been compared to the work of modern sculptors like Noguchi and Brancusi\"; \"the most popular day use destination in Voyageurs National Park.\" 5 miles by boat from the Kabetogama Lake Visitor Center (nps.gov getting around)."},{"name":"Houseboating in Voyageurs (NPS permit)","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/planyourvisit/houseboating.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","family","romance"],"booking_route":"Recreation.gov houseboat permit (recreation.gov/permits/251977)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":4,"blurb":"\"Houseboats are required to have a permit for overnight use\"; \"There is a $15 nightly fee in additional to a $10 reservation service fee per transaction\"; designated sites carry fire rings and mooring posts, undesignated sites must be \"at least 200 yards from developed areas\", two houseboats per site. \"All houseboat rentals are commercially operated by companies located just outside the park''s boundaries.\""},{"name":"Frontcountry boat-in campsites","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/planyourvisit/camping.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","family","wildlife"],"booking_route":"Recreation.gov (Voyageurs National Park camping permits)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":5,"blurb":"\"137 sites are located on the park''s large lakes and are directly accessible from any park boat launch\"; \"all camping types require a reservation/permit\" and \"All tent campsites within Voyageurs National Park require a reservation fee and nightly amenity fees\". Bear-proof food lockers at campsites hold two 48-quart coolers."},{"name":"Grand Tour on the Voyageur (ranger-led)","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/planyourvisit/guided-tours.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["wildlife","family","senior"],"booking_route":"Recreation.gov \"VNP Boat Tours\" or 1-877-444-6777","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":6,"blurb":"From the Rainy Lake Visitor Center: \"Grand Tour (2.5 hrs)\" - \"Wildlife and scenery focused, cultural/historic narratives included\"; and \"Life on the Lake Tour (2.5 hrs)\" to gold-mine and fish-camp sites with a ranger-led hike. NPS vessels are accessible."},{"name":"North Canoe Voyage","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/planyourvisit/guided-tours.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","culture","adventure"],"booking_route":"Recreation.gov \"VNP Special Interpretive Programs\"","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":7,"blurb":"A special interpretive programme of \"1 hour on land and 1/2 hour on the water\" (1.5 hours in all) in a voyageur-style North canoe; minimum age 8; from the Rainy Lake and Ash River visitor centers."},{"name":"Kettle Falls Dam and historic crossing","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/learn/historyculture/kettlefalls.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culture","adventure"],"booking_route":"none needed - reached by private boat, water taxi or ranger tour","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":8,"blurb":"\"Many centuries ago, Kettle Falls was a main artery of the travel route along the wilderness border region. Native peoples gathered, hunted, and speared sturgeon at the falls, voyageurs paddled and portaged through the area\"; the dams were begun around 1910, and the hotel built by timber cruiser Ed Rose has hosted travellers \"since 1913\" - bought in 1918 \"for $1,000 and four barrels of whiskey.\" 13 miles by boat from the Ash River Visitor Center."},{"name":"Kettle Falls Hotel dining room","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/planyourvisit/eatingsleeping.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","culture"],"booking_route":"walk-in by boat; hotel phone 218-240-1724","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":9,"blurb":"\"The only location to purchase food within Voyageurs National Park is at the Kettle Falls Hotel\"; \"The Kettle Falls Hotel has a restaurant that offers full sit-down meals for breakfast, lunch, and dinner\" - about 15 miles from the nearest road and only reachable by watercraft."},{"name":"Rainy Lake and Kabetogama ice roads","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/planyourvisit/winter-activities.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","motoring","family"],"booking_route":"none needed - free; check the weekly Winter Ice and Trail Conditions Report","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":10,"blurb":"Winter roads on the frozen lakes: the \"Rainy Lake Ice Road begins at the visitor center boat launch\" and the \"Kabetogama Lake Ice Road connects the Ash River and Kabetogama Lake Visitor Centers\"; \"open to cars and trucks of less than 7,000 lbs. gross vehicle weight. Snowmobiles are not permitted on the ice road\"; 30 mph limit; \"conditions vary yearly\"."},{"name":"Groomed snowmobile trails","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/planyourvisit/winter-activities.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","motoring"],"booking_route":"none needed - free trails; snowmobile rentals from CUA holders","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":11,"blurb":"\"110 miles of staked and groomed trails for snowmobiling\" on frozen lakes and designated safety portages only; land areas are off-limits except for safety portages and \"hill climbing is prohibited.\""},{"name":"Snowshoe and ski rental, Rainy Lake Visitor Center","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/planyourvisit/winter-activities.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","family","hiking"],"booking_route":"walk-up at the Rainy Lake Visitor Center","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["gear","activities"],"draw_rank":12,"blurb":"\"From January through March, the Rainy Lake Visitor Center offers rentals Friday-Monday, 10am-4pm\": \"$10 per pair for adults / $5 for children 16 & under\" - traditional wooden snowshoes and cross-country skis with boots and poles."},{"name":"Bear-resistant food storage (NPS kit)","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/planyourvisit/bears-and-food-storage.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","adventure","wildlife"],"booking_route":"affiliate retail referral (BearVault via AvantLink; REI.com via AvantLink)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":5,"commission_pct_high":8,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":13,"blurb":"About 150 black bears live in the park. The NPS: \"Secure food and other scented items at all times by using bear lockers or bear-resistant cans\"; food must be stored \"in a park bear-proof food locker, in a certified bear-proof cooler or canister according to manufacturer''s instructions, hung from a backcounbtry bear pole, or hung fourteen feet from the ground\". The kit this asks for is a certified bear canister or bear-proof cooler."},{"name":"EPA-approved bear pepper spray (NPS kit)","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/planyourvisit/bears-and-food-storage.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","adventure","wildlife"],"booking_route":"affiliate retail referral (Counter Assault via AvantLink)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":8,"commission_pct_high":8,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":14,"blurb":"\"Bear pepper spray can be used defensively to stop an aggressive bear in Voyageurs. Human pepper spray and bear pepper spray are not the same. Make sure you select an EPA approved product that is specifically designed to stop bears. It has no repellent properties, so do not apply it to your equipment.\""},{"name":"Boat safety kit: PFDs, whistle, GPS, first aid (NPS kit)","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/planyourvisit/boat-safety.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","family"],"booking_route":"affiliate retail referral (REI.com via AvantLink; Amazon Associates)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":3,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":15,"blurb":"The NPS boating checklist: \"one wearable U.S. Coast Guard approved personal flotation device (PFD) on board and accessible for each person in the watercraft\" (state law, canoes and kayaks included); \"a whistle or horn capable of producing a continuous sound for two seconds\"; \"handy to have a handheld GPS device\"; \"Flashlight and first aid kit: In-case of emergency have the essentials on board.\""},{"name":"Water treatment for lake water (NPS kit)","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/planyourvisit/safety.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","adventure","family"],"booking_route":"affiliate retail referral (REI.com via AvantLink; Amazon Associates)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":3,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":16,"blurb":"\"Thinking of Drinking the Water? Always treat lake water before using it for drinking or cooking.\" The kit this asks for is a filter, purifier or treatment tablets."},{"name":"Dark Sky Park and northern lights viewing","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/learn/nature/northern-lights.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["wildlife","romance","family"],"booking_route":"none needed - free, open year-round","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":17,"blurb":"A designated Dark Sky Park; the two designated viewing areas are \"The Meadwood Road Day Use Area\" on the Ash River Visitor Center road and \"the upper parking lot at the Rainy Lake Visitor Center\". The aurora \"can appear any time of year. However, Voyageurs winters provide longer periods of darkness, which can increase your chances\"."},{"name":"Fishing the park''s 30 named lakes","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/fishing.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","wildlife","family"],"booking_route":"none needed in the park - a Minnesota fishing licence is required (Minnesota DNR)","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":18,"blurb":"\"Fish abound in the 30 named lakes, which consist of four large lakes and 26 smaller interior lakes\"; \"Fifty-four fish species\", including Walleye, Sauger, Northern Pike and Smallmouth Bass. \"Visitors fishing within Voyagers National Park must obtain a State of Minnesota Fishing license.\""},{"name":"Backcountry camping and interior-lake canoes","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/planyourvisit/boat-rentals.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","hiking","wildlife"],"booking_route":"Recreation.gov backcountry permit","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay","gear"],"draw_rank":19,"blurb":"Backcountry sites \"require travel by water to a remote trailhead, but then visitors must hike\"; \"The park rents canoes and kayaks on its other interior lakes (e.g., Locator Lake, Little Shoepack Lake) through its backcountry camping program.\""},{"name":"Kab-Ash Trail primitive campsites","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/planyourvisit/eatingsleeping.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","adventure"],"booking_route":"Recreation.gov permit (\"all camping types require a reservation/permit\")","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":20,"blurb":"\"All campsites in Voyageurs are only accessible by watercraft, with the exception of two hike-in primitive campsites along the Kab-Ash Trail\" - camping \"that incorporates hiking and backpacking without needing a boat\". Pets are not allowed at the Kab-Ash primitive sites (NPS pets page)."},{"name":"Rainy Lake Visitor Center","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/planyourvisit/hours.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior"],"booking_route":"none needed - free; park headquarters (218) 283-6600","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":21,"blurb":"Summer \"9 a.m. - 5 p.m., 7-days a week\"; \"October 1-31, 2026: 10 a.m.-4 p.m.\"; home port of the Voyageur tour boat, start of the Rainy Lake ice road, winter rentals, the accessible first 1/4 mile of the Oberholtzer Trail, and a designated dark-sky viewing lot."},{"name":"Ash River Visitor Center (historic Meadwood Lodge)","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/planyourvisit/hours.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","culture"],"booking_route":"none needed - free","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":22,"blurb":"\"Historic Meadwood Lodge now serves as Ash River Visitor Center\"; summer \"9 a.m. - 5 p.m., 7-days a week\", last day of the 2026 season \"September 27, 2026\", reopening \"May 29, 2027\". 13 miles by boat to Kettle Falls (nps.gov getting around)."},{"name":"Rainy Lake Houseboats","source":"https://www.rainylakehouseboats.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","family","romance"],"booking_route":"own website \"Book Now\" or 800-554-9188","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":23,"blurb":"International Falls (2031 County Road 102): \"9 Houseboat Styles\" on Rainy Lake \"in Voyageurs National Park - the only inland water-based park in the National Park System\", with fishing for walleye, smallmouth bass, northern pike, crappie and musky; also runs VNP tours and fishing guides. 1-800-554-9188."},{"name":"Voyagaire Lodge & Houseboats, Crane Lake","source":"https://www.voyagaire.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","family","romance"],"booking_route":"own website (Checkfront) or (218) 317-8388","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":24,"blurb":"\"Largest Fleet of Houseboat Rentals in Minnesota\" - \"With 34 houseboats available\"; an \"Assistant Captain\" can guide first-timers from the dock; plus lodge rooms, dining, boat, UTV and snowmobile rentals and a fishing guide service. \"The Gateway to Voyageurs National Park - Crane Lake, Minnesota.\""},{"name":"Northernaire Houseboats","source":"https://www.northernairehouseboats.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","family","romance"],"booking_route":"own website reservations or 218-286-5221","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":25,"blurb":"2690 County Road 94, International Falls: \"11 different types of houseboats\" from the 2-person Explorer to the 12-person Aurora (\"Luxury\"); season \"from May to September, weather permitting\"; Rainy Lake \"is the largest lake in Voyageurs National Park spanning 73 miles in one direction.\""},{"name":"Voyageurs Outfitters","source":"https://www.voyageursoutfitters.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","wildlife","family"],"booking_route":"FareHarbor (own website)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities","gear"],"draw_rank":26,"blurb":"A CUA holder listed by the NPS for Rainy Lake and Kabetogama boat rentals: the full-day Kettle Falls boat tour (\"From $ 274.19\", 6 hours, 6 passengers) and a two-hour Grand Boat Tour; kayak rental \"Paddle and PFD included\", canoe packages with \"a 16'' NovaCraft fiberglass canoe\" and two PFDs, SUPs, fishing boats, pontoons, snowshoe rental and water taxis."},{"name":"Rainy Lake Aquatics","source":"https://www.rainylakeaquatics.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","family"],"booking_route":"call or text 218-216-7885","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":27,"blurb":"Ranier: \"Canoe, Kayak & Paddleboard Rentals\" by the day or for multiple days, with \"youth rentals\", \"angler equipment\", tandem kayaks and 2- and 3-seat canoes \"to paddle to one of the many amazing camp sites\"; water taxi for renters with Rainy Lake Charters. Listed by the NPS as a Rainy Lake rental CUA holder."},{"name":"Wilderness Inquiry - Voyageurs Family Canoe","source":"https://www.wildernessinquiry.org/trips/voyageurs-national-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","group","adventure","wildlife"],"booking_route":"own website trip booking","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"guide","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":28,"blurb":"Five days from the Ash River Visitor Center, \"Price $ 765 (Adult)\", up to 15 people; \"youth travel at 25% less than adults\"; includes guides, campfire meals, \"Equipment for all outdoor activities\", shared tents and park permits and fees. Day 1 paddles into Kabetogama Lake to camp on Bald Rock. A CUA holder on the NPS guided-trips list."},{"name":"Ash Riviera Resort","source":"https://new.ashriviera.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["motoring","adventure","family"],"booking_route":"phone 218 393-4598 or ashriviera12@gmail.com","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":29,"blurb":"10351 Ash River Trail, Orr: \"gateway to the Voyageurs National Park\"; \"a few rustic, fully equipped cabins with private decks\" and \"RV sites with full hook-ups, bathroom facilities and laundry on-site\"; rental boats for \"a relaxing cruise around the islands or to Kettle Falls\". Listed by the NPS for Kabetogama/Ash River boat rentals."},{"name":"Rainy Lake RV Campground","source":"https://rainylake.org/lodging-item/rainy-lake-rv-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["motoring","family","adventure"],"booking_route":"phone 218-288-1130","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":30,"blurb":"2967 MN 11E, International Falls: \"a private 32 acre compound on the shores of Rainy Lake\" with \"40x50 full hookup sites that include sewer, 20/30/50 amp electricity, water, a dock slip, fish cleaning facility\"; nightly, weekly, monthly and seasonal stays; private beach next to Bohman''s Boat Landing. 218-288-1130."},{"name":"Voyageurs RV Campground by Venserra","source":"https://www.hipcamp.com/en-US/land/minnesota-voyageurs-rv-campground-by-venserra-06yh8xr8","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["motoring","family"],"booking_route":"Hipcamp","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":31,"blurb":"International Falls: \"spacious RV sites equipped with both 30- and 50-amp electrical service, as well as water and sewer hookups\" - three full-hookup sites for rigs of 30-45 feet, pull-throughs, restrooms, pet-friendly; \"Within a 30-minute drive from the Rainy Lake Visitor Center\". Reviews on the listing report bathrooms and showers needing attention."},{"name":"City Beach Campground, International Falls","source":"https://www.ci.international-falls.mn.us/services/parks-facilities/city-beach/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","adventure"],"booking_route":"City of International Falls (terms on the city page; booking method not read)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":32,"blurb":"3405 County Road 46, \"3 miles east of International Falls\": \"650 feet of sand beach on Rainy Lake\", a covered picnic pavilion, grills, dressing and bathroom facilities, a floating swim platform and \"Camp Sites - tents only\". Named by the NPS as the city''s public campground for visitors without a boat."},{"name":"Woodenfrog and Ash River state forest campgrounds","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/planyourvisit/camping-in-gateway-communities.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","adventure"],"booking_route":"Minnesota DNR (dnr.state.mn.us - not fetched, HTTP 403)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":33,"blurb":"\"In the Kabetogama and Ash River area, the Minnesota Department of Natural Resources (DNR) offers two nearby facilities: Woodenfrog State Forest Campground (Kabetogama) Ash River State Forest Campground (Ash River)\" - the NPS''s answer for car and tent campers without a watercraft. The DNR facility pages refused the fetch (HTTP 403), so site counts and fees are not stated here."},{"name":"16 Squared Cabin, Nett Lake","source":"https://www.hipcamp.com/en-US/land/minnesota-16-squared-cabin-6p0h9lol","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["glamping","family","wildlife"],"booking_route":"Hipcamp","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":34,"blurb":"Host Amanda N. describes a \"Glamp\" on 160 acres of pine forest, fields and a pond with miles of trails: a cabin for 5 with two sets of bunkbeds, wood-burning stove, firewood, outhouse, picnic table, porch grill, potable water in jugs; no electricity, Wi-Fi or running water; pets on leash. 98% recommend (116 ratings)."},{"name":"Cantilever Distillery and Hotel, Ranier","source":"https://www.cantileverdistillery.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["romance","culinary","culture"],"booking_route":"own website \"BOOK NOW\" (Wyndham Trademark Collection)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay","eat"],"draw_rank":35,"blurb":"\"Just steps away from Rainy Lake and minutes from Voyageurs National Park\": \"31 hotel rooms\" with claw-foot tubs, a rooftop sauna and hot tub, and a cocktail room pouring its own Minnesota-grain bourbon, gin and vodka. \"We are excited to announce our partnership with Wyndham Hotels® as the newest boutique hotel in the Trademark Collection.\""},{"name":"AmericInn by Wyndham International Falls","source":"https://rainylake.org/lodging-item/americinn-by-wyndham/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior"],"booking_route":"wyndhamhotels.com (brand booking; linked from the listing, not fetched)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":36,"blurb":"2500 Keenan Drive: \"free breakfast and WiFi, an indoor pool, and hot tub\"; \"dog-friendly, non-smoking\"; \"three miles from Falls International Airport (INL)\" and three miles from the Canadian border crossing to Fort Frances. HotelGuides lists 85 rooms and suites over 4 floors. Its Northern Lights Pub hosts a free soup-and-chili guest reception Sunday-Thursday."},{"name":"Days Inn by Wyndham International Falls","source":"https://rainylake.org/lodging-item/days-inn/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family"],"booking_route":"wyndhamhotels.com/days-inn (brand booking; not fetched) or 800-329-7466","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":37,"blurb":"2331 Highway 53 South, International Falls; 218-283-9441. HotelGuides lists it \"1 mile from Falls Airport\", 2 floors and 57 rooms with no elevator, exercise room and free continental breakfast."},{"name":"The Thunderbird","source":"https://rainylake.org/lodging-item/thunderbird-lodge/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","family","romance"],"booking_route":"own website reservations (thunderbirdmn.com)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":38,"blurb":"Serving guests \"since 1937\", \"just across Highway 11 from the Voyageurs National Park Rainy Lake Visitors Center\" - \"the closest and most convenient basecamp for all year-round park activities\"; 54 acres with 1,200 feet of Rainy Lake shoreline and \"15 renovated lodge rooms\"."},{"name":"Thunderbird Dining Room & Lounge","source":"https://thunderbirdmn.com/fine-dining","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","romance"],"booking_route":"own website reservations","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":39,"blurb":"\"Our world-class Dining Room has a renowned reputation and beautiful views of Rainy Lake. Executive Chef John Barnes creates amazing signature dishes and daily specials\"; breakfast, lunch, dinner and pizza menus, and a lakeside cocktail lounge with \"a full-service copper top bar\" and \"large stone fireplace\"."},{"name":"Cantilever Cocktail Room","source":"https://www.cantileverdistillery.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","romance"],"booking_route":"walk-in; own website","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":40,"blurb":"\"Enjoy a cocktail made with our in house craft spirits made from the finest local ingredients. Order a flight of bites\"; distillery tours of \"Minnesota-distilled bourbon, gin, and vodka\" made \"using the finest Minnesota grains and water from the Canadian Shield.\""},{"name":"The Falls Bistro at the Cobblestone","source":"https://rainylake.org/thing-to-do/falls-bistro-at-the-cobblestone/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary"],"booking_route":"phone 218-324-4660 (thefallsbistro.com)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":41,"blurb":"Inside the Cobblestone Hotel & Suites, 1 Memorial Dr, International Falls: \"chef-inspired American fare\" - poutine, burgers, steak and seafood, bourbon salmon - with handcrafted cocktails; opens at 4 PM. 218-324-4660."},{"name":"Chocolate Moose Restaurant Co.","source":"https://www.chocolatemooserestaurant.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in; online ordering on the own website","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":42,"blurb":"\"An icon in the Borderland of International Falls\": \"hearty portions\" for breakfast, lunch and dinner - pancakes, omelets, \"our ever-popular Monte Cristo sandwich\", burgers, pastas, wraps and specialty dinners."},{"name":"Sha Sha Resort Bar & Grill","source":"https://rainylake.org/lodging-item/sha-sha-resort-on-rainy-lake/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in; phone 218-286-3241","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":43,"blurb":"\"At the end of the road on Rainy Lake, about 10 miles east of International Falls\": large lakeside decks, \"famous Long Island iced teas and nachos\", a gift shop, cabins, and the chipmunk-feeding tradition. 1664 Highway 11 East; 218-286-3241."},{"name":"Loony''s Brew, Ranier","source":"https://rainylake.org/thing-to-do/loonys-brew/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary"],"booking_route":"walk-in","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":44,"blurb":"\"On the shores of Rainy Lake in Ranier\", next to Cantilever: craft beer, spirits, wine, lattes, smoothies, non-alcoholic brews and pizzas, with \"live music, events, and lake views from the deck\". 3481 Main St; 218-540-1001."},{"name":"Boondock''s Bar & Grill + RV Campground, Ray","source":"https://rainylake.org/thing-to-do/boondocks-bar-and-grill/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","motoring"],"booking_route":"walk-in; phone (218) 875-2700","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat","stay"],"draw_rank":45,"blurb":"On Highway 53 in Ray: food with patio seating in summer, Bingo Thursdays at 6 pm, Mexican Night Wednesdays at 5 pm, and \"An on-site RV campground available\"; a stop on the ATV and snowmobile trails. Closed Mondays and Tuesdays. 4660 US-53; (218) 875-2700."},{"name":"Gateway General Store, Kabetogama","source":"https://www.kabetogama.com/eat","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","culinary"],"booking_route":"walk-in","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat","shop"],"draw_rank":46,"blurb":"\"A true Northwoods general store with a little bit of everything - groceries, gifts, bait, licenses, and more\"; locally loved ice cream and take-and-bake pizza. 9378 Highway 53; (218) 875-2121."},{"name":"Island View Lodge & Cabins","source":"https://rainylake.org/lodging-item/island-view-lodge-cabins/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","family"],"booking_route":"email via the listing (booking method not read)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay","eat"],"draw_rank":47,"blurb":"On Rainy Lake: \"15 cabin rentals and lodge rooms\", a meal and cocktail \"overlooking Rainy Lake and Voyageurs National Park\", and \"a full-service marina with floating docks and boat rentals\"."},{"name":"Sandberg''s Idlewild Resort, Kabetogama","source":"https://idlewildresort.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","adventure"],"booking_route":"own website booking form or 218-248-2291","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":48,"blurb":"\"Enjoy the Beauty of Voyageurs National Park in Complete Comfort\": cabins with private bathrooms, full kitchens and sun decks, a heated pool and spa, protected boat harbor with full dock service, \"Kayaks and Paddle Boards\" and boat rentals; family and dog friendly. Now booking summer 2027."},{"name":"Voyageurs Conservancy","source":"https://www.voyageurs.org/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["wildlife","hiking","family"],"booking_route":"programmes and shop via the own website","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"guide","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities","shop"],"draw_rank":49,"blurb":"\"Voyageurs Conservancy is the official nonprofit partner of Minnesota''s national park\"; it funded many of the park''s night-sky-friendly lights (NPS Dark Sky page), is listed by the NPS for guided hiking and environmental education, and sells Voyageurs-inspired apparel supporting park projects."}],"faq":[{"q":"Can you camp at Voyageurs National Park?","a":"Yes, with a permit. \"137 sites are located on the park''s large lakes and are directly accessible from any park boat launch\"; there are also backcountry sites reached by boat and trail and \"Two hike-in campsites along the Kab-Ash Trail that don''t require a boat.\" \"All camping types require a reservation/permit\" on Recreation.gov.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/planyourvisit/camping.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you visit Voyageurs National Park without a boat?","a":"Partly. \"The park''s visitor centers and some trails can be reached by car, but much of its beauty is best explored by boat.\" Without a boat you can take the ranger-led tour boats from the Rainy Lake and Kabetogama/Ash River visitor centers (mid-June to end of September), or use \"Local businesses with valid Commercial Use Authorizations\" that rent watercraft and run water taxis.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/planyourvisit/directions.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you rent a houseboat at Voyageurs National Park?","a":"Not from the park: \"Voyageurs National Park does not have houseboats available for rent but there are several commercial options in the gateway communities\" serving the Rainy Lake and Namakan districts, including Crane Lake. Every houseboat needs an NPS overnight permit - \"$15 nightly fee in additional to a $10 reservation service fee per transaction\".","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/planyourvisit/eatingsleeping.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Are there boat tours in Voyageurs National Park?","a":"Yes. From the Rainy Lake Visitor Center the Voyageur runs the \"Grand Tour (2.5 hrs)\", \"Life on the Lake Tour (2.5 hrs)\" and \"Kettle Falls Cruise (6.5 hrs)\"; from Kabetogama/Namakan the Ne-Zho-Dain runs a 5.5-hour Kettle Falls Tour, Life on the Lake and Ellsworth Rock Gardens. Season \"mid-June through the end of September\"; tickets on Recreation.gov from April 15 at 9am, or 1-877-444-6777.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/planyourvisit/guided-tours.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Does Voyageurs National Park have an entrance fee?","a":"No: \"Voyageurs National Park does not have an entrance fee.\" Fees apply to tent campsites (\"a reservation fee and nightly amenity fees\"), houseboat permits, ranger-led boat tours, special interpretive programmes, winter equipment rentals and special use permits.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/planyourvisit/fees.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Is Voyageurs National Park open?","a":"\"It is open and free to visit year-round.\" Visitor center hours vary: Ash River, Kabetogama Lake and Crane Lake closed for the season after September 27, 2026 and reopen May 29, 2027; Rainy Lake Visitor Center is open \"October 1-31, 2026: 10 a.m.-4 p.m., 7 days a week\".","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/planyourvisit/hours.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Do you need bear spray in Voyageurs National Park?","a":"The NPS does not require it, but says \"Bear pepper spray can be used defensively to stop an aggressive bear in Voyageurs\" and to choose \"an EPA approved product that is specifically designed to stop bears.\" About 150 black bears live in the park; what is required is food storage - in a bear-proof locker, a certified bear-proof cooler or canister, or hung 14 feet up.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/planyourvisit/bears-and-food-storage.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you fish in Voyageurs National Park?","a":"Yes. \"Fish abound in the 30 named lakes\" and \"Fifty-four fish species have been identified\", including Walleye, Sauger, Northern Pike and Smallmouth Bass. \"Visitors fishing within Voyagers National Park must obtain a State of Minnesota Fishing license\", and fishing follows Minnesota law except for the park-specific rules on bait and campsites.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/fishing.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Is Voyageurs National Park dog friendly?","a":"In set places. Pets are allowed at frontcountry campsites and day-use sites, on lake surfaces where motorboats are allowed, outside visitor centers and on the Rainy Lake Visitor Center Recreation Trail; not on backcountry sites on the Kabetogama Peninsula, at the Kab-Ash primitive sites, on tour boats, inside visitor centers or on other trails. Leash \"not exceeding six feet in length\".","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/planyourvisit/pets.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"What is the closest airport to Voyageurs National Park?","a":"\"Falls International Airport is located in International Falls, Minnesota. Taxi service and rental cars are available here. Most flights entering the area will pass through the larger Minneapolis-St. Paul airport located about 5 hours south\". \"There is no public transportation to Voyageurs National Park.\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/voya/planyourvisit/gettingaround.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Voyageurs National Park: Houseboats, Boat Tours & Kettle Falls | TravelWell","meta_description":"Free entry, 137 boat-in campsites, ranger boat tours to Kettle Falls, houseboat fleets on Rainy and Crane lakes, ice roads, and dark skies for the aurora.","slug":"voyageurs-national-park-minnesota","primary_keyword":"Voyageurs National Park","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination"},"hero":{"query":"Voyageurs National Park houseboat Rainy Lake"}}'::jsonb, 52)
