":"published","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":26,"blurb":"Booking.com: \"Featuring 3-star accommodations, Hampton Inn & Suites Kenosha Pleasant Prairie is located in Kenosha, 16 miles from Six Flags Great America and 7.7 miles from Dinosaur Discovery Museum.\" Hilton''s own page was not fetched."},{"name":"Candlewood Suites Kenosha - Pleasant Prairie by IHG","source":"https://www.booking.com/city/us/kenosha.html","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family"],"booking_route":"ihg.com (brand booking; not fetched) or Booking.com","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":27,"blurb":"Booking.com: \"Featuring barbecue facilities, Candlewood Suites Kenosha - Pleasant Prairie by IHG offers rooms in Kenosha, 6.6 miles from Dinosaur Discovery Museum and 9.5 miles from Carthage College.\" IHG''s own page was not fetched."},{"name":"The Inn On Sheridan","source":"https://www.booking.com/city/us/zion.html","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["romance","senior"],"booking_route":"Booking.com","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":4,"commission_pct_high":4,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":28,"blurb":"Booking.com: \"Located in Zion, 1.4 miles from Illinois Beach State Park\"; guest score 8.7/10. The property''s own site was not fetched."},{"name":"DICK''S Sporting Goods Gurnee Mills","source":"https://stores.dickssportinggoods.com/il/gurnee/1340/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","family","hiking"],"booking_route":"walk-in store; online at dickssportinggoods.com","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":9.25,"commission_pct_high":9.25,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear","shop"],"draw_rank":29,"blurb":"6140 West Grand Avenue, Gurnee Mills, Gurnee, IL 60031: \"Enjoy the outdoors with camping gear, bikes, outdoor games and quality kayaks for sale. Stay ready for the elements with outerwear from top brands like The North Face and Patagonia.\""},{"name":"DICK''S Sporting Goods Kenosha","source":"https://stores.dickssportinggoods.com/wi/kenosha/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in store; online at dickssportinggoods.com","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":9.25,"commission_pct_high":9.25,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear","shop"],"draw_rank":30,"blurb":"\"DICK''s Sporting Goods Shops Of Prarie Ridge, 9899 76th Street, Shops Of Prarie Ridge, Kenosha, WI 53158\" (store #753), per the retailer''s own store locator."},{"name":"Franks Diner","source":"https://www.franksdinerkenosha.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","culture","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in; phone 262-657-1017 for parties of 6+","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":31,"blurb":"Kenosha, WI: \"We''ve been flipping eggs and tossing sass since 1926\"; \"Home of the World-Famous Garbage Plate\"; Monday-Friday 6:00 AM-1:30 PM, Saturday 7:00 AM-1:30 PM, Sunday 7:00 AM-12:30 PM; reservations by phone \"for parties of six or more, with at least one day''s notice\". 262.657.1017."},{"name":"House of Gerhard","source":"https://www.houseofgerhard.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","culture"],"booking_route":"phone 262-694-5212","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":32,"blurb":"Kenosha: \"SINCE 1965\", \"AUTHENTIC GERMAN CUISINE AND AMERICAN FAVORITES\" - \"From hearty sausages to delectable schnitzels, there''s something for everyone to enjoy.\" 262-694-5212."},{"name":"Big Star Drive-In","source":"https://www.bigstardrivein.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family","culture"],"booking_route":"drive-in, carhop service; nothing to book","commission_status":"none","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":33,"blurb":"Kenosha: \"Big Star Drive-in was opened in the Spring of 1954 by Roy and Marian Boehner serving up made to order burgers, fries and shakes with carhop service. Now three generations later it''s still going strong.\""},{"name":"Kenosha Brewing Company","source":"https://www.kenoshabrewingcompany.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","culture"],"booking_route":"walk-in; private parties by phone 262-694-9494","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":34,"blurb":"4017 80th Street, Kenosha: \"Over 90 years ago local Monks from the area perfected their craft of making great beer at the very location KBC occupies today\"; beer flights of \"4 snifter glasses of 5 oz. pours\"; closed Monday-Tuesday, Wednesday-Thursday 3PM-10:30PM, Friday 3PM-11:00PM, Saturday 11AM-11:00PM, Sunday 11AM-5:00PM. 262-694-9494."},{"name":"Mars Cheese Castle","source":"https://www.marscheese.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in; online store for shipping","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat","shop"],"draw_rank":35,"blurb":"2800 West Frontage Rd., Kenosha, WI: cheese, spreads, bakery, meats and souvenirs, with a restaurant kitchen and tavern; store \"9am-7pm Daily\", kitchen Mon-Fri 11am-7pm and Sat-Sun 9am-7pm, tavern 11am-7pm daily. 1-855-352-MARS (6277)."},{"name":"Tenuta''s Deli","source":"https://www.tenutasdeli.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","wine","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in or online order","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat","shop"],"draw_rank":36,"blurb":"\"A Kenosha Tradition Since 1950\" - \"Your Shortest Route to Italy\": an Italian deli and grocery with \"a vast variety of wine, spirits, and beer from around the world\"; online ordering. (262) 657-9001."}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Illinois Beach State Park free?","a":"Entry is free, but the beach carries a small fee. IDNR: \"The Illinois Department of Natural Resources does not charge an Entrance Fee to any state owned or operated land with the exception of Wildlife Prairie Park and sites with beaches. Beaches charge a $1 a day per person for beach use only.\"","source":"https://dnr.illinois.gov/parks/camp/faqcamping.html","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"What is camping like at Illinois Beach State Park?","a":"The campground has \"220 Class A Premium sites with electricity and access to showers and sanitary facilities\" and is \"open from April 1 through Nov. 15\". \"Reservations can be made up to 180 days in advance\" through ExploreMoreIL; \"Unreserved campsites are available on a first-come, first-serve basis.\" Sites have no individual water or sewer hookups, but there are water hydrants and a dump station.","source":"https://dnr.illinois.gov/parks/camp/park.adelinejaygeo-karisillinoisbeach.html","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Does Illinois Beach State Park have showers?","a":"Yes, in the campground: its 220 sites have \"electricity and access to showers and sanitary facilities\", and \"Five handicap accessible campsites are present in the campground near the shower buildings.\"","source":"https://dnr.illinois.gov/parks/camp/park.adelinejaygeo-karisillinoisbeach.html","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you swim at Illinois Beach State Park?","a":"Yes: \"Swimming is a major summertime attraction along the sandy shorelines, and both units provide ample parking.\" But \"there are no on-duty lifeguards, so please be careful.\"","source":"https://dnr.illinois.gov/parks/activity/park.adelinejaygeo-karisillinoisbeach.html","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you fish at Illinois Beach State Park?","a":"Yes: \"Fishing is allowed along the beach area in both units (except in the swimming areas) and there are several small inland fishing ponds, including Sand Pond, where a disabled fishing pier is available.\"","source":"https://dnr.illinois.gov/parks/activity/park.adelinejaygeo-karisillinoisbeach.html","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you bring dogs to Illinois Beach State Park?","a":"Yes, but not everywhere: \"Dogs are not allowed on the beach or in the nature preserve. Dogs are allowed in the campground, the picnic area, and the remainder of the trails as long as they are on a leash. Pets are not to be left unattended.\"","source":"https://dnr.illinois.gov/parks/picnic/park.adelinejaygeo-karisillinoisbeach.html","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you drink at Illinois Beach State Park?","a":"No. \"Alcohol is prohibited at Illinois Beach State Park.\" The camping page adds: \"No Possession or Consumption of Alcohol allowed on any site in the Campground.\"","source":"https://dnr.illinois.gov/parks/picnic/park.adelinejaygeo-karisillinoisbeach.html","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Where is Illinois Beach State Park?","a":"In Zion, IL 60099, \"stretching 6.5 miles along the sandy shore of Lake Michigan in northern Illinois.\" From the south: \"I-294 north to Rt 173 east (approx. 8 miles) to Sheridan Road. Make a right on Sheridan Road to Wadsworth Road, make a left, and you will be in the park.\" Park office 847-662-4811.","source":"https://dnr.illinois.gov/parks/park.adelinejaygeo-karisillinoisbeach.html","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Is there a resort at Illinois Beach State Park?","a":"Yes. The Illinois Beach Resort and Conference Center (Illinois Beach Hotel) is \"Located directly on the shores of Lake Michigan\"; IDNR calls it \"the only hotel in the state that is nestled along the sandy beaches of Lake Michigan.\" It is open year round, with Nolan''s Restaurant Wednesday-Sunday 4:00-8:00 pm.","source":"https://dnr.illinois.gov/parks/lodge/park.adelinejaygeo-karisillinoisbeach.html","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"What is there to do at Illinois Beach State Park?","a":"IDNR lists \"swimming, boating, picnicking, hiking, fishing, camping, and simply appreciating nature.\" The South Unit has \"5 miles of trails, including a 2.2-mile loop trail with a graveled surface\"; in the north, \"Camp Logan Trail is a 1.8-mile multi-use loop\"; the Zion Bike Trail links the two units.","source":"https://dnr.illinois.gov/parks/activity/park.adelinejaygeo-karisillinoisbeach.html","accessed":"2026-10-03"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Illinois Beach State Park: Lake Michigan Beach, Dunes & Camping | TravelWell","meta_description":"6.5 miles of Lake Michigan shore in Zion, IL: dunes, the first Illinois Nature Preserve, a 220-site campground, the beach hotel and where to stay nearby.","slug":"illinois-beach-state-park-illinois","primary_keyword":"Illinois Beach State Park","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination"},"hero":{"query":"Illinois Beach State Park dunes Lake Michigan"}}'::jsonb, 54),
  ('indiana-dunes-state-park-indiana', '12A', 'Indiana Dunes State Park', 'United States', 'Indiana''s tallest dunes on Lake Michigan', 'future', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'The Great Lakes', '{"hiking","family","wildlife","adventure","parks"}', '{"coastal","family-friendly","adventurous","historic"}', '{}', null, null, '{"safety":{"posture":"book-freely","source":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/usa","verified":"2026-10-08"},"jewels":[{"name":"3 Dune Challenge (Trail 8)","source":"https://www.in.gov/dnr/state-parks/programs/fitness/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","adventure","family","sports"],"booking_route":"none needed - inside the park; vehicle entrance fee applies","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":1,"blurb":"\"Challenge yourself, your friends, and your family to climb the three tallest sand dunes in the park any day of the year.\" A \"1.5-mile self-guided challenge trail\" from the nature center, \"the toughest trail in the park, with 552 vertical feet to climb\"; the reward is \"a free 3-Dune Conqueror sticker from Indiana Dunes Tourism.\""},{"name":"Indiana Dunes State Park beach","source":"https://www.in.gov/dnr/state-parks/parks-lakes/indiana-dunes-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior"],"booking_route":"none needed - inside the park; vehicle entrance fee applies","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":2,"blurb":"Lake Michigan \"Swimming / Beach\" with \"Mobility mats for easy beach access\"; \"Dogs are not allowed on the Indiana Dunes State Park beach.\" The DNR''s \"Swim at Your Own Risk policy is in effect at all beaches except at Indiana Dunes State Park.\""},{"name":"Mt. Tom","source":"https://www.indianadunes.com/blog/post/our-guide-to-the-3-dune-challenge/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","adventure"],"booking_route":"none needed - on Trail 8 inside the park","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":3,"blurb":"Indiana Dunes Tourism: \"Mt. Tom (192 feet): The tallest dune offers a rewarding climb with a well-maintained staircase\"; with Mt. Jackson (176 feet) and Mt. Holden (184 feet) it makes up the 3 Dune Challenge, which \"Most hikers complete ... in 45-75 minutes.\""},{"name":"Dunes Pavilion - Jonna''s Beach Cafe & Rooftop","source":"https://dunespavilion.com","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family","romance"],"booking_route":"walk-in; reservations and events by phone 219-250-2568 or dunespavilionevents.com","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":4,"blurb":"\"Established in 1930, this gem features an event space, restaurant & grill, ice cream shop and amazing views from the rooftop\"; Beach Cafe 11AM-5PM and Rooftop 4PM-9PM, closed Wednesdays, \"Weather permitting\"; 1600 N 25 E, Chesterton; (219) 250-2568. The park gate fee applies to reach it."},{"name":"Indiana Dunes State Park Campground","source":"https://www.in.gov/dnr/state-parks/parks-lakes/indiana-dunes-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","group","motoring","hiking"],"booking_route":"indianastateparks.reserveamerica.com","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":5,"blurb":"\"Electric - 140 (all 50 amp service)\" plus a \"Youth Tent Area\", reserved through the Indiana State Parks reservation site. The DNR publishes campground and youth tent area maps."},{"name":"Trail 9","source":"https://www.in.gov/dnr/state-parks/parks-lakes/indiana-dunes-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","wildlife"],"booking_route":"none needed - park trail","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":6,"blurb":"\"MODERATE (3.75 miles)-Provides the best representative view of the dunes.\""},{"name":"Trail 10 and the Big Blowout","source":"https://www.in.gov/dnr/state-parks/parks-lakes/indiana-dunes-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","adventure","wildlife"],"booking_route":"none needed - park trail","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":7,"blurb":"\"MODERATE (5.5 miles)-Hikers are rewarded by stands of white pine and a ''tree graveyard'' in Big Blowout.\" The longest trail on the DNR''s list."},{"name":"Indiana Dunes State Park Nature Center","source":"https://www.in.gov/dnr/state-parks/parks-lakes/indiana-dunes-state-park/nature-center-and-events","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","wildlife","senior"],"booking_route":"none needed - inside the park","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":8,"blurb":"\"Open daily, 9 a.m.-4 p.m. CT (closed on major state holidays)\"; interpretive naturalist services and events, 219-926-1390; the 3 Dune Challenge trail \"begins at the nature center\"."},{"name":"Accessible bird observation tower","source":"https://www.in.gov/dnr/state-parks/parks-lakes/indiana-dunes-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["wildlife","senior"],"booking_route":"none needed - inside the park","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":9,"blurb":"\"Birding (Dunes Birding Blog). Accessible bird observation tower available.\" The DNR links the Indiana Dunes birding blog from the park page."},{"name":"Trail 2","source":"https://www.in.gov/dnr/state-parks/parks-lakes/indiana-dunes-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","senior","wildlife"],"booking_route":"none needed - park trail","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":10,"blurb":"\"EASY (3 miles)-The best trail for early spring flowers and ferns.\""},{"name":"Trail 7","source":"https://www.in.gov/dnr/state-parks/parks-lakes/indiana-dunes-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","family"],"booking_route":"none needed - park trail","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":11,"blurb":"\"MODERATE (1.1 miles)-Similar to Trail 4. Most direct route from Nature Center to the beach.\""},{"name":"Trails 3 and 4","source":"https://www.in.gov/dnr/state-parks/parks-lakes/indiana-dunes-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","wildlife","family"],"booking_route":"none needed - park trails","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":12,"blurb":"Trail 3: \"MODERATE (.75 mile)-Provides an opportunity to view succession in the dunes area.\" Trail 4: \"MODERATE (.75 mile)-Goes through dunes covered with black oak forest.\""},{"name":"Indiana Dunes Centennial Challenge","source":"https://www.in.gov/dnr/state-parks/programs/fitness/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culture","family","hiking"],"booking_route":"none needed - self-guided inside the park","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":13,"blurb":"\"This adventure takes you throughout the park. Explore the park''s unique history by visiting each stop and taking a photo at each location.\""},{"name":"Cross-country ski trails","source":"https://www.in.gov/dnr/state-parks/parks-lakes/indiana-dunes-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","hiking"],"booking_route":"none needed - bring your own skis","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":14,"blurb":"\"Cross-country Skiing (trails available, no ski rental)\"; the DNR publishes a cross-country ski trail map for the park."},{"name":"Smelt fishing","source":"https://www.in.gov/dnr/state-parks/parks-lakes/indiana-dunes-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure"],"booking_route":"none needed in the park (state licensing not read in this build)","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":15,"blurb":"The DNR lists fishing at the park as \"Fishing (Smelt Only)\"."},{"name":"Kit for the dune climb: water and sunscreen","source":"https://www.indianadunes.com/blog/post/our-guide-to-the-3-dune-challenge/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","family","adventure"],"booking_route":"retail referral - REI.com via AvantLink (merchant 10248)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":5,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":16,"blurb":"For the 3 Dune Challenge Indiana Dunes Tourism says to bring \"Plenty of water, sunscreen, insect repellent, and snacks\", and notes \"Running or walking on sand is 1.6x more difficult than on solid ground!\" The DNR rates Trail 8 \"RUGGED\". The DNR''s own park page publishes no kit list."},{"name":"Kit for the trails: insect repellent and tick checks","source":"https://www.indianadunes.com/blog/post/dunes-101-how-to-stay-safe-in-the-dunes/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","family"],"booking_route":"retail referral - Amazon Associates","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":3,"commission_pct_high":4,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":17,"blurb":"Indiana Dunes Tourism''s safety guide: \"Be sure to wear insect repellent\" and \"Tuck your pants into your socks, and check for ticks after hiking.\""},{"name":"Kit for the water: a life jacket","source":"https://www.indianadunes.com/blog/post/dunes-101-how-to-stay-safe-in-the-dunes/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","family"],"booking_route":"retail referral - REI.com via AvantLink (merchant 10248)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":5,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":18,"blurb":"\"Be sure to wear a life jacket or other personal flotation device when paddling on the lakes, rivers, and streams.\" On rip currents: \"Even the strongest swimmers cannot fight a rip current, so be sure to always heed warning signs.\" The DNR: \"Please be aware of rip currents and large waves that can occur while swimming and boating.\""},{"name":"Indiana Dunes National Park","source":"https://www.nps.gov/indu/index.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","wildlife","family"],"booking_route":"national park entrance fee (see its own dossier)","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":19,"blurb":"The separate federal park around the state park: \"these 15 miles of Indiana coast. Over 50 miles of trails lead through shifting sand dunes, quiet woodlands, sunny prairies and lush wetlands\" across \"the park''s 16,000 acres.\" Its own dossier carries its jewels."},{"name":"Indiana Dunes Visitor Center","source":"https://www.indianadunes.com/blog/post/our-guide-to-the-3-dune-challenge/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","hiking"],"booking_route":"none needed - walk-in visitor centre","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities","shop"],"draw_rank":20,"blurb":"Run by Indiana Dunes Tourism at 1215 N State Road 49, Porter, +1(219) 926-2255: \"Stop by the Indiana Dunes Visitor Center to pick up your free 3 Dune Challenge sticker or purchase a commemorative t-shirt.\""},{"name":"Michigan City Campground","source":"https://www.michigancitycampground.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["motoring","family"],"booking_route":"own website (Staylist booking engine) or phone","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":21,"blurb":"1601 US-421, Michigan City, (219) 872-7600: cabin camping, RV campsites with \"water, electric, and sewer\" hookups and concrete patios, tent lots, and a \"pool, shop, playground, bathhouse\"; booked online at booking.staylist.app/michigancity."},{"name":"Weko Beach Campground","source":"https://www.campspot.com/park/weko-beach-campground","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","adventure"],"booking_route":"Campspot","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":3,"commission_pct_high":3,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":22,"blurb":"5239 Lake St., Bridgman, MI: \"a sandy shoreline on beautiful Lake Michigan\" with \"68 campsites, and 11 rustic cabins\", kayak rentals, boat launch, showers, dump station and snack stand. Campspot lists it 33 miles from Chesterton."},{"name":"Oak Lake RV Resort yurts and cabins","source":"https://www.campspot.com/park/oak-lake-rv-resort-fair-oaks-in","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["glamping","family","motoring"],"booking_route":"Campspot","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":3,"commission_pct_high":3,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":23,"blurb":"5310 E 900 N, Fair Oaks: \"68 beautiful acres\" with yurts and cottage rentals, deluxe and primitive cabins, 55 RV sites with 20/30/50-amp full hookups and 13 tent sites; \"the sandy beach overlooking the lake\", a waterpark and dog park. Campspot lists it 35 miles from Chesterton."},{"name":"Fairfield Inn and Suites Valparaiso","source":"https://www.indianadunes.com/places-to-stay/hotels-and-inns/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior"],"booking_route":"marriott.com (brand booking; not fetched)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":8,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":24,"blurb":"Listed by Indiana Dunes Tourism under its Valparaiso hotels as a Marriott property. Marriott''s own page was not fetched, so nothing else about the property is stated here."},{"name":"Hampton Inn Portage","source":"https://www.indianadunes.com/places-to-stay/hotels-and-inns/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior"],"booking_route":"hilton.com (brand booking; not fetched)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":25,"blurb":"Listed by Indiana Dunes Tourism under Portage: \"Five miles from Lake Michigan beaches\". Hilton''s own page was not fetched, so nothing else about the property is stated here."},{"name":"Holiday Inn Express & Suites Portage","source":"https://www.indianadunes.com/places-to-stay/hotels-and-inns/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","motoring"],"booking_route":"ihg.com (brand booking; not fetched)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":26,"blurb":"Listed by Indiana Dunes Tourism under Portage, \"Off I-94 and Highway 20\". IHG''s own page was not fetched, so nothing else about the property is stated here."},{"name":"Spring House Inn","source":"https://www.indianadunes.com/places-to-stay/hotels-and-inns/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","hiking"],"booking_route":"own booking (not read)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":27,"blurb":"Listed by Indiana Dunes Tourism among the Duneland Communities hotels, in Porter. Its own page was not fetched in this build."},{"name":"Camp Stop General Store & Beach Shop","source":"https://www.southshorecva.com/blog/post/explore-the-south-shores-water-trails-part-1-for-beginners/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in rental at the store (own site unreachable)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["gear","shop"],"draw_rank":28,"blurb":"Beverly Shores, on the Indiana Dunes shoreline: South Shore Convention & Visitors Authority lists it for renting \"bikes, kayaks or paddle boards\". Its own site did not resolve when fetched."},{"name":"Rogers-Lakewood Park boat rentals","source":"https://visitindiana.in.gov/blog/post/kayak-paddleboard-beginner/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","adventure"],"booking_route":"on-site rental at the park","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["gear","activities"],"draw_rank":29,"blurb":"Valparaiso: Visit Indiana lists rentals from a \"rowboat for $5/hour to a paddleboat or itBike for $5/half hour\"; the South Shore CVA page lists \"rowboat for $6 an hour to a paddleboat for $6 per half an hour\" - the two pages disagree on price."},{"name":"Lucrezia Cafe and Ristorante","source":"https://www.lucreziacafe.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","romance"],"booking_route":"walk-in; parties of 8+ phone ahead","commission_status":"none","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":30,"blurb":"428 S. Calumet, Chesterton, (219) 926-LUCY: \"innovative Northern Italian specialties\" in \"a relaxed and eclectic atmosphere\"; Sun-Thurs 11am-9pm, Fri-Sat 11am-10pm; \"Reservations are not accepted at this time at our Chesterton or Crown Point locations.\""},{"name":"Running Vines Winery","source":"https://www.indianadunes.com/locals-love-top-10-date-night-restaurants/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["wine","romance","culinary"],"booking_route":"not read (own site returned no content)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":31,"blurb":"Chesterton: Indiana Dunes Tourism - \"wines made right here in Porter County\" with flatbreads and cold plates for sharing."},{"name":"Don Quijote Restaurante and Imports","source":"https://www.indianadunes.com/locals-love-top-10-date-night-restaurants/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","romance","wine"],"booking_route":"not read","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":32,"blurb":"Valparaiso: Indiana Dunes Tourism - \"The best and most authentic Spanish restaurant outside of Spain\" (its quoted billing), with tapas, paella, desserts and Spanish wines."},{"name":"Radius","source":"https://www.indianadunes.com/locals-love-top-10-date-night-restaurants/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","entertainment"],"booking_route":"not read","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":33,"blurb":"Valparaiso: Indiana Dunes Tourism - \"innovative cocktails and live weekend entertainment\" with a Greek-American menu of \"comfortably cool\" dishes."},{"name":"Stacks Bar and Grill","source":"https://www.indianadunes.com/locals-love-top-10-date-night-restaurants/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary"],"booking_route":"not read","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":34,"blurb":"Valparaiso: Indiana Dunes Tourism - a \"casual library-themed atmosphere\" with rooftop dining overlooking downtown and a \"vibrant and creative menu.\""},{"name":"Wagner''s Ribs","source":"https://www.indianadunes.com/locals-love-top-10-date-night-restaurants/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary"],"booking_route":"not read","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":35,"blurb":"Indiana Dunes Tourism - \"award-winning fall-off-the-bone ribs and tasty sides\"; a 21-and-over venue."},{"name":"Shoreline Brewery","source":"https://southshorecva.com/restaurants/restaurants-near-the-dunes/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary"],"booking_route":"not read","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":36,"blurb":"Michigan City: listed by the South Shore Convention & Visitors Authority among restaurants near the dunes for craft beer and food. Its own site showed only an age gate."},{"name":"Zorn Brew Works","source":"https://southshorecva.com/restaurants/restaurants-near-the-dunes/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary"],"booking_route":"not read","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":37,"blurb":"Michigan City: listed by the South Shore Convention & Visitors Authority among restaurants near the dunes as a craft brewery with menu options."},{"name":"Stop Zero Beach Cantina","source":"https://southshorecva.com/restaurants/restaurants-near-the-dunes/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family"],"booking_route":"not read","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":38,"blurb":"Michigan City: listed by the South Shore Convention & Visitors Authority as located on the beach at Washington Park."}],"faq":[{"q":"How much is Indiana Dunes State Park?","a":"Per vehicle per day: \"$7 - noncommercial vehicles with Indiana license plates\" and \"$20 - noncommercial vehicles with out-of-state license plates, every day, including holidays.\" A \"$50 Annual Entrance Pass\" and a \"$120 Non-resident Annual Entrance Pass\" are also sold.","source":"https://www.in.gov/dnr/state-parks/rates-and-fees/entrance-fees","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you camp at Indiana Dunes State Park?","a":"Yes. The DNR lists \"Electric - 140 (all 50 amp service)\" campsites and a \"Youth Tent Area\", with reservations at indianastateparks.reserveamerica.com.","source":"https://www.in.gov/dnr/state-parks/parks-lakes/indiana-dunes-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Does Indiana Dunes State Park have full hookups?","a":"The DNR''s park page lists the campground as \"Electric - 140 (all 50 amp service)\" and does not mention water or sewer hookups at the sites. Check the electric campground map on the DNR page or the reservation listing before booking.","source":"https://www.in.gov/dnr/state-parks/parks-lakes/indiana-dunes-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Does Indiana Dunes State Park allow dogs?","a":"Not on the swimming beach: \"Dogs are not allowed on the Indiana Dunes State Park beach.\" Indiana Dunes Tourism adds that \"if they are on a six-foot leash, they can be on the other parts of the beach\" outside the swimming beach.","source":"https://www.in.gov/dnr/state-parks/parks-lakes/indiana-dunes-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you swim at Indiana Dunes State Park?","a":"Yes - the park lists \"Swimming / Beach\" on Lake Michigan, and \"During the summer, swimming hours may change because of weather and staffing.\" It is the one Indiana state park beach not under the \"Swim at Your Own Risk\" policy, and children 12 and younger \"must be supervised by someone aged 16 or older.\"","source":"https://www.in.gov/dnr/state-parks/rates-and-fees/miscellaneous-fees","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you fish at Indiana Dunes State Park?","a":"Only for smelt: the DNR lists the activity as \"Fishing (Smelt Only)\".","source":"https://www.in.gov/dnr/state-parks/parks-lakes/indiana-dunes-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"What time zone is Indiana Dunes State Park in?","a":"\"Indiana Dunes State Park is in the Central Time Zone, one hour behind Eastern Time.\"","source":"https://www.in.gov/dnr/state-parks/parks-lakes/indiana-dunes-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"How many acres is Indiana Dunes State Park?","a":"\"Indiana Dunes consists of 2,182 acres of primitive, beautiful, historic, and unique Hoosier landscape.\"","source":"https://www.in.gov/dnr/state-parks/parks-lakes/indiana-dunes-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Where is Indiana Dunes State Park located?","a":"At \"1600 N. 25 E. Chesterton, IN 46304\", on Lake Michigan in northwest Indiana.","source":"https://www.in.gov/dnr/state-parks/parks-lakes/indiana-dunes-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"What is the difference between Indiana Dunes State Park and the national park?","a":"Ownership and rules: \"The National Park is owned by the United States Government''s Department of the Interior. The State Park is owned by the State of Indiana''s Department of Natural Resources (DNR).\" The state park charges \"$7 for in-state vehicles and $20 for out-of-state vehicles\", and pets are allowed on national park beaches but not on the state park swimming beach.","source":"https://www.indianadunes.com/plan-your-visit/faq/","accessed":"2026-10-03"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Indiana Dunes State Park: 3 Dune Challenge, Mt. Tom & Beach | TravelWell","meta_description":"Climb Mt. Tom on the 1.5-mile 3 Dune Challenge, swim the Lake Michigan beach, camp at 140 electric sites, and find RV parks, yurts and hotels nearby.","slug":"indiana-dunes-state-park-indiana","primary_keyword":"Indiana Dunes State Park","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination"},"hero":{"query":"Indiana Dunes State Park Mt. Tom dune Lake Michigan"}}'::jsonb, 55)
