etched - HTTP 403)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":33,"blurb":"Listed by HotelGuides at \"2850 Columbus Street, I-80, Exit 90, Ottawa, IL 61350\", \"9 miles from Starved Rock State Park\". IHG''s own page refused the fetch (HTTP 403), so nothing else about the property is stated here."},{"name":"Holiday Inn Express & Suites Peru","source":"https://hotelguides.com/attraction-maps/illinois/map-hotels-near-starved-rock-state-park-il.html","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior"],"booking_route":"ihg.com (brand booking; not fetched - HTTP 403)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":34,"blurb":"Listed by HotelGuides at \"5253 Trompeter Road, I-80, Exit 75, Peru, IL 61354\", \"8 miles from Starved Rock State Park\". IHG''s own page refused the fetch (HTTP 403), so nothing else about the property is stated here."},{"name":"Skoogs Pub & Grill","source":"https://www.starvedrockcountry.com/2026/05/22/dining-tour-of-starved-rock-country/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in (no booking method read)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":35,"blurb":"155 Mill St., North Utica: \"generous portions and craveable meals\" - the \"3/4-pound Skoog Burger\" and wings \"in multiple sauces\" (Starved Rock Country tourism board)."},{"name":"Bruce & Ollie''s Ice Cream, Specialty Coffee & Deli","source":"https://www.starvedrockcountry.com/2026/05/22/dining-tour-of-starved-rock-country/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in (no booking method read)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":36,"blurb":"166 Mill St., North Utica: \"hand-scooped ice cream, coffee drinks and light fare\" in \"a historic building with original stone walls and exposed beams\" (Starved Rock Country tourism board)."},{"name":"August Hill Winery & Illinois Sparkling Co.","source":"https://www.starvedrockcountry.com/2026/05/22/dining-tour-of-starved-rock-country/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["wine","romance","culinary"],"booking_route":"walk-in tasting room (no booking method read)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat","shop"],"draw_rank":37,"blurb":"106 Mill St., North Utica: \"award-winning wines made from grapes grown in the region\"; wine flights, patio seating and sparkling and still wines to take home (Starved Rock Country tourism board). The augusthill.com domain is listed for sale, so no own page was read."},{"name":"Uptown Grill","source":"https://www.starvedrockcountry.com/2026/05/22/dining-tour-of-starved-rock-country/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","romance","wine"],"booking_route":"not read","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":38,"blurb":"601 1st St., La Salle: char-broiled steaks \"cut and aged in-house\", prime rib on Friday and Saturday nights, seafood and oysters \"prepared fresh every day\", \"more than 100 wines and 12 craft beers on tap\" (Starved Rock Country tourism board)."},{"name":"HAZE Smokehouse","source":"https://www.starvedrockcountry.com/2026/05/22/dining-tour-of-starved-rock-country/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","entertainment"],"booking_route":"not read","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":39,"blurb":"59 Bucklin St., La Salle: \"slow-smoked meats\", house-made sauces and an \"extensive bourbon selection\", with an outdoor performance space where \"blues and blues rock\" are the specialty (Starved Rock Country tourism board)."},{"name":"Hank''s Farm Restaurant","source":"https://www.starvedrockcountry.com/2026/05/22/dining-tour-of-starved-rock-country/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family"],"booking_route":"not read","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":40,"blurb":"2973 Route 71, Ottawa: dining \"inside a converted dairy barn surrounded by rolling acreage and roaming animals\", known for its Sunday brunch buffet, with outdoor dining and a full bar (Starved Rock Country tourism board)."},{"name":"The Beach House","source":"https://www.starvedrockcountry.com/2026/05/22/dining-tour-of-starved-rock-country/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","romance"],"booking_route":"not read","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":41,"blurb":"700 La Salle St., Ottawa: \"a globally inspired coastal menu features fresh oysters, tuna poke and an authentic lobster roll\", plus a full bar and extensive wine list (Starved Rock Country tourism board)."},{"name":"CatsEye Wine Bar","source":"https://www.starvedrockcountry.com/2026/05/22/dining-tour-of-starved-rock-country/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["wine","romance"],"booking_route":"not read","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":42,"blurb":"724 La Salle St., Ottawa: \"an intimate venue known for its extensive selection of local and international wines\", with art openings, live music and tastings (Starved Rock Country tourism board)."}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Starved Rock State Park free?","a":"Yes. The IDNR answers: \"The wonderful thing about Illinois is that all state parks are free for everyone to enjoy.\" Camping, the Lodge and the Lodge''s tours carry their own charges.","source":"https://dnr.illinois.gov/content/dam/soi/en/web/dnr/parks/documents/starvedrock-common-park-qa.pdf","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you camp at Starved Rock State Park?","a":"Yes, only in the state campground: \"Camping is only allowed at designated campsites at the Starved Rock State Park Campground located south of the park off Route 71\". It has \"133 Class-A Premium campsites. Electric hook-up only\", and \"RESERVATIONS ARE REQUIRED\", made online at recreation.exploremoreil.com 6 months to 4 days ahead.","source":"https://dnr.illinois.gov/parks/camp/park.starvedrock.html","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you swim at Starved Rock State Park?","a":"No: \"Swimming, wading, or sliding in any water bodies, including rivers, canyon creeks, and waterfalls, is not allowed.\" Fines begin at $195.","source":"https://dnr.illinois.gov/parks/activity/park.starvedrock.html","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you bring dogs to Starved Rock State Park?","a":"Yes: \"Dogs are permitted in the park as long as they are leashed, their owners clean up after them, dispose of waste properly, and ensure they have enough water while hiking.\" They may not drink from canyon waterfalls, creeks or the river, and \"Dogs are not permitted on guided hikes or programs.\"","source":"https://dnr.illinois.gov/parks/activity/park.starvedrock.html","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you kayak at Starved Rock State Park?","a":"Yes, on the Illinois River. \"The optimal location for launching your boat is at the Lone Point Shelter area, situated along Route 71 on the eastern side of the park\"; \"Kayak and canoe rental is not available at the park.\" The IDNR''s Q&A adds that \"Kayak Starved Rock manages all kayak rentals and tours out of Lone Point Shelter\".","source":"https://dnr.illinois.gov/parks/activity/park.starvedrock.html","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you bike at Starved Rock State Park?","a":"Not on its trails: \"Bikes are not allowed on the trails at Starved Rock due to the fragile sandstone geology, but you can travel just 2 miles south of the park to the Matthiessen Vermillion River Area (NOT allowed at the Dells area of Matthiessen) at Matthiessen State Park where there are biking trails to enjoy!\"","source":"https://dnr.illinois.gov/content/dam/soi/en/web/dnr/parks/documents/starvedrock-common-park-qa.pdf","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you fly a drone at Starved Rock State Park?","a":"No: \"Drones are not allowed at Starved Rock State Park due to the number of visitors on the trails, picnic area, and overlooks, and the disturbance to wildlife such as the park''s nesting bald eagle population.\"","source":"https://dnr.illinois.gov/content/dam/soi/en/web/dnr/parks/documents/starvedrock-common-park-qa.pdf","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Why is it called Starved Rock State Park?","a":"\"The name Starved Rock State Park is derived from a Native American legend\": after Chief Pontiac was killed in 1769, a group of Illinois \"sought refuge atop a 125-foot sandstone butte, which is now known as Starved Rock\" and were encircled by the Ottawa and Potawatomi. The IDNR adds: \"This is just a tale though and not supported by any archaeological evidence or historical documentation.\"","source":"https://dnr.illinois.gov/parks/about/park.starvedrock.html","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"What should I wear to Starved Rock State Park?","a":"It depends on the season, per the IDNR: in winter \"Traction devices such as micro cleats or Yaktrax on hiking boots are highly recommended\"; in spring \"Waterproof hiking shoes are highly recommended, and a change of dry socks and clean shoes for the ride home\"; in summer \"pack plenty of water for themselves and their pets\".","source":"https://dnr.illinois.gov/content/dam/soi/en/web/dnr/parks/documents/starvedrock-common-park-qa.pdf","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"What is the best time to visit Starved Rock State Park?","a":"The IDNR gives the seasons by what you want to see: waterfalls \"occur March through June but, may dry out late June through October\"; \"Fall colors typically peak the 2nd to 3rd week of October\"; icefalls form \"in the month of January\", when eagles concentrate below the lock and dam. The busiest time is \"Friday through Sunday from 11-3\" between mid-March and early November.","source":"https://dnr.illinois.gov/content/dam/soi/en/web/dnr/parks/documents/starvedrock-common-park-qa.pdf","accessed":"2026-10-03"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Starved Rock State Park: Canyons, Waterfalls & the Lodge | TravelWell","meta_description":"Free entry, 18 sandstone canyons and 13 miles of trails, spring waterfalls, January eagles, the 1930s Lodge, and where to camp, glamp and stay nearby.","slug":"starved-rock-state-park-illinois","primary_keyword":"Starved Rock State Park","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination"},"hero":{"query":"Starved Rock State Park canyon waterfall"}}'::jsonb, 56),
  ('warren-dunes-michigan', '12A', 'Warren Dunes State Park', 'United States', 'Lake Michigan dunes rising 260 feet', 'future', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'The Great Lakes', '{"hiking","family","adventure","wine","parks"}', '{"coastal","adventurous","family-friendly"}', '{}', null, null, '{"safety":{"posture":"book-freely","source":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/usa","verified":"2026-10-08"},"jewels":[{"name":"The dunes and three miles of Lake Michigan shoreline","source":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260801110517/https://www.michigan.gov/recsearch/parks/WarrenDunes","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","family","adventure","wildlife"],"booking_route":"none needed beyond a Recreation Passport for vehicle entry","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":1,"blurb":"\"Its rugged dune formation, rising 260 feet above the lake, offers spectacular views\"; \"3 miles of shoreline\" and \"an extensive network of richly forested dunes, large open dunes and interdunal wetlands.\""},{"name":"Buoyed swim beach and day-use area","source":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260801110517/https://www.michigan.gov/recsearch/parks/WarrenDunes","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior","ocean"],"booking_route":"none needed - Recreation Passport for vehicle entry","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":2,"blurb":"\"A buoyed swim area is located along the day-use area on Lake Michigan\"; three accessible bathroom buildings with foot showers and bottle fillers; three 100-foot accessible walkways; two beach/aqua wheelchairs to borrow; \"five picnic areas located along the main entrance road\". The DNR warns \"state parks do not have lifeguards\"."},{"name":"Six miles of dune and forest trails","source":"https://swmichigan.org/member/warren-dunes-state-park","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","wildlife","family"],"booking_route":"none needed - free park trails","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":3,"blurb":"DNR: \"6 miles of hiking trails\". Visit Southwest Michigan: \"most are moderately difficult and all offer photo-worthy scenery. You can hike the trails all year, but the best months are March to November\"; \"Foot trails range from ⅓ mile to one mile long.\""},{"name":"Mt. Randall Modern Campground","source":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260801110517/https://www.michigan.gov/recsearch/parks/WarrenDunes","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","motoring","hiking"],"booking_route":"MiDNRReservations.com or 800-447-2757","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":4,"blurb":"182 sites in two loops, \"shady and sunny, and some are wooded\"; tagged electrical service, pull-through sites, some 50-amp, toilet and shower building, playground. 2026 rates table: $60 full hook-up, $50 50-amp, $45 20/30-amp; reservable May 1 - October 21."},{"name":"Third Coast Paddling, Warren Dunes rentals","source":"https://www.thirdcoastpaddling.com/location/warren-dunes-state-park","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","family","ocean"],"booking_route":"own website online booking, walk-ins if available","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities","gear"],"draw_rank":5,"blurb":"The in-park rental station (the DNR calls it Third Coast Surf) \"on the north side of the park, just past the far end of the parking lot, and right next to the dog beach\": \"Single / DOUBLE KayakS,\" \"Stand-Up Paddleboards,\" \"Loungeboards,\" and \"Sandboards / Sand Sleds\"; \"10AM - 6PM EST Sat/Sun\" from \"Memorial Day Weekend through early October\"; rentals from \"$25 per hour\" with life jackets included. (269) 468-9399."},{"name":"Warren Dunes Rustic Mini Cabins","source":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260801110517/https://www.michigan.gov/recsearch/parks/WarrenDunes","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","glamping"],"booking_route":"MiDNRReservations.com or 800-447-2757","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":6,"blurb":"\"There are three rustic cabins in Mt. Randall campground. Each cabin sleeps six people and includes two full-size beds and two single bunk beds\"; ceramic heater, electricity, deck, fire pit and cook grill - Pine (#5), Oak (#51) and Hemlock (#65). 2026 rates table: $80; reservable May 1 - October 21."},{"name":"Warren Dunes Hildebrandt Semi-Modern Campground","source":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260801110517/https://www.michigan.gov/recsearch/parks/WarrenDunes","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","family"],"booking_route":"MiDNRReservations.com or 800-447-2757","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":7,"blurb":"37 sites, \"more rustic and offers a relaxing atmosphere. Most sites are sunny and open, while some are wooded\"; \"There is no electrical service available\"; vault toilets, with Mt. Randall''s shower buildings \"just a five-minute walk away\". 2026 rates table: $40; reservable May 1 - October 21."},{"name":"The dog beach","source":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260801110517/https://www.michigan.gov/recsearch/parks/WarrenDunes","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","hiking"],"booking_route":"none needed - Recreation Passport for vehicle entry","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":8,"blurb":"\"Pets are allowed north of the northernmost swim buoy at the beach, providing 2.5 miles of shoreline open to pets. Pets must always be on a 6-foot leash and under an owner''s immediate control.\""},{"name":"Hang gliding and sandboarding the dunes","source":"https://swmichigan.org/member/warren-dunes-state-park","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure"],"booking_route":"permit from park staff, 269-426-4013","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":9,"blurb":"DNR: the dune \"is excellent for hang gliding (permit is required)\". Visit Southwest Michigan: \"Hang glide off towering dunes; request a required permit from the park staff\" and \"Rocket down tall dunes on your sandboard.\""},{"name":"Coast Guard-approved life jackets","source":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260603183713/https://www.michigan.gov/dnr/education/safety-info/beach-safety","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","ocean","adventure"],"booking_route":"affiliate referral to a gear retailer (REI.com via AvantLink)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":5,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":10,"blurb":"The kit the DNR tells beach visitors to bring: \"We also highly recommend bringing U.S. Coast Guard-approved life jackets—especially for children, new swimmers, and anyone less confident in the water\", because \"state parks do not have lifeguards\". Warren Dunes is on the DNR''s list of buoyed Great Lakes swim beaches."},{"name":"Weko Beach Campground","source":"https://www.campspot.com/c/rv-camping-in-michigan/near-warren-dunes-state-park","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","motoring","ocean"],"booking_route":"Campspot (campspot.com/park/weko-beach-campground)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":3,"commission_pct_high":3,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["stay","gear"],"draw_rank":11,"blurb":"Campspot: 3 miles straight-line, Bridgman - \"a sandy shoreline on beautiful Lake Michigan! Including 68 campsites, and 11 rustic cabins\"; \"a seasonal boat launch, kayak rentals, picnic areas, and a playground\"; \"head over next door and check out Warren Dunes State Park\". 4.3 from 194 verified reviews."},{"name":"Tabor Hill Winery & Restaurant","source":"https://taborhill.com/restaurant/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["wine","culinary","romance"],"booking_route":"own website reservations","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":12,"blurb":"Buchanan: \"pairs award-winning Michigan wines with seasonally inspired cuisine\"; \"Recently recognized by Wine Enthusiast as one of the 57 Best Winery Restaurants in the World\"; head chef Justin Carlisle; restaurant Thursday-Saturday 12-9 pm, Sunday 12-6 pm, closed Monday-Wednesday. (269) 422-1161."},{"name":"Lemon Creek Winery","source":"https://lemoncreekwinery.com/visit-us/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["wine","culinary","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in tasting room","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat","shop"],"draw_rank":13,"blurb":"Berrien Springs: \"Our 165-year-old historic farm sits on over 300 rolling acres of vineyards and orchards. Open year-round\"; \"12 flights to choose from in the summer and 8 flights in the winter. Each flight comes with five 2oz. pours\"; U-pick fruit and a farm market. Hours Monday-Friday 11am-6pm, Saturday 10am-6pm, Sunday 12pm-6pm."},{"name":"Warren Woods State Park","source":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260606041550/https://www.michigan.gov/recsearch/parks/WarrenWoods","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","wildlife"],"booking_route":"none needed - Recreation Passport for vehicle entry","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":14,"blurb":"\"a 311-acre nature preserve and hidden gem just 7 minutes from Warren Dunes State Park\" with \"a towering beech and majestic maple forest and the meandering Galien River\"; \"a quiet, 1-mile trail that follows the scenic river\"; the Elm Valley Road entrance closes in winter."},{"name":"Beach food trucks and Big Springs Souvenir Shop","source":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260801110517/https://www.michigan.gov/recsearch/parks/WarrenDunes","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family"],"booking_route":"walk-up","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat","shop"],"draw_rank":15,"blurb":"\"The Big Springs Souvenir Shop – located in the beach building – sells T-shirts, sweatshirts, ice cream, snacks and more.\" \"There are five food trucks (hamburgers, hotdogs, ice cream, tacos, slushies, smoothies and more) located in the beach parking lot May through Labor Day weekend.\""},{"name":"Grand Mere State Park","source":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260606045435/https://www.michigan.gov/recsearch/parks/GrandMere","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","wildlife"],"booking_route":"none needed - Recreation Passport for vehicle entry","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":16,"blurb":"\"magnificent sand dunes, deep blowouts and half a mile of Lake Michigan shoreline, accessible by the park''s two trails. Two inland lakes lie behind the dunes\"; bluegill fishing on South and Middle lakes; a track chair to borrow at no cost. \"Hunting activities occur along the Dune Trail during designated seasons.\""},{"name":"Hickory Creek Winery","source":"https://www.hickorycreekwinery.com/contact","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["wine","romance"],"booking_route":"own website reservation request","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":17,"blurb":"750 Browntown Road, Buchanan: \"Traditional guided tasting of 5 wines - $15 per person\" or a 5-wine flight board; tasting room and patio; \"We do it all by hand, bucket-by-bucket.\" Open daily (Sat 11am-7pm, Sun-Thu 12-5pm, Fri 12-6pm). (269) 422-1100."},{"name":"Nature programs and the Explorer program","source":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260801110517/https://www.michigan.gov/recsearch/parks/WarrenDunes","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","wildlife"],"booking_route":"none needed - check the park''s explorer program calendar","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":18,"blurb":"\"Seasonal naturalists offer nature-based programming at the park during the summer and/or fall\"; \"The park also offers weekly nature programs not listed in the online calendar.\""},{"name":"Winter on the dunes","source":"https://swmichigan.org/member/warren-dunes-state-park","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","hiking","family"],"booking_route":"none needed - Recreation Passport for vehicle entry","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":19,"blurb":"\"Sled and snowboard on the dunes.\" \"Cross-country ski on a three-mile loop that takes you through a beautiful, wooded area behind the Great Warren Dunes. Or snowshoe on the dunes and other trails.\" \"Photograph ice formations and snowy vistas.\""},{"name":"Warren Dunes Youth Group-Use Campground","source":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260801110517/https://www.michigan.gov/recsearch/parks/WarrenDunes","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["group","family"],"booking_route":"phone the park, 269-426-4013","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":20,"blurb":"\"This rustic group campground is available for groups up to 100. There are six sites that include picnic table and fire pit. There is a hand pump for water.\" 2026 rates table: \"$20/group of 6\", year-round. Reserve by calling the park, 269-426-4013."},{"name":"Linens and cookware for the mini cabins","source":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260801110517/https://www.michigan.gov/recsearch/parks/WarrenDunes","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","glamping"],"booking_route":"affiliate referral to a gear retailer (Sea to Summit via AvantLink)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":21,"blurb":"The kit the DNR tells cabin guests to bring: \"You must provide your own linens and cookware.\" The cabin supplies a \"waist-high cook grill (only cooking unit provided)\"."},{"name":"Shamrock Park RV Park - Berrien Springs","source":"https://www.campspot.com/c/rv-camping-in-michigan/near-warren-dunes-state-park","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["motoring","family"],"booking_route":"Campspot (campspot.com/park/shamrock-park-rv-park-berrien-springs-mi)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":3,"commission_pct_high":3,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":22,"blurb":"Campspot: 14 miles straight-line; \"a picturesque retreat nestled along the scenic St. Joseph River\" near U-pick fruit farms and the Berrien County Youth Fair; starting at $40.00; 4.8 from 39 verified reviews."},{"name":"Wandering Soul Cabin, Sawyer","source":"https://glampinghub.com/unitedstatesofamerica/midwest/michigan/sawyer/cabin-rental-getaway-lake-michigan/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["glamping","romance"],"booking_route":"Glamping Hub enquiry / availability check","commission_status":"none","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_basis":"published","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":23,"blurb":"Glamping Hub: \"located just a short drive away from the shores of Lake Michigan about half a mile from charming downtown\" Sawyer; \"About five minutes down the road from the property, glampers will find Warren Dunes State Park\"; check-in 03:00 PM; \"Smoking and pets are not allowed.\" New listing, no reviews."},{"name":"Glamping Get Away bell tent, Niles","source":"https://glampinghub.com/unitedstatesofamerica/midwest/michigan/niles/niles-rental-best-romantic-getaways-in-michigan/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["glamping","romance","family"],"booking_route":"Glamping Hub enquiry / availability check","commission_status":"none","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_basis":"published","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":24,"blurb":"Glamping Hub: \"Bell tent in Niles, MI\", \"4 guests • 1 bedroom • 3 beds • 1 bathroom\", \"located near the Saint Joseph River\"; composting toilet; pets on leash; check-in 02:00-11:00 PM; 4.8 from 3 reviews."},{"name":"Courtyard by Marriott St. Joseph Benton Harbor","source":"https://swmichigan.org/member/courtyard-by-marriott","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior","wine"],"booking_route":"marriott.com (brand booking; not fetched)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":8,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":25,"blurb":"1295 Cinema Way, Benton Harbor, 269-210-3000, as listed by Visit Southwest Michigan: The Bistro, indoor pool and fitness centre; \"a short drive to ... Silver Beach, Lake Michigan, and many other great attractions like local wineries, Warren Dunes, and the Kids Museum.\" Marriott''s own page was not fetched (brand sites refuse automated reads)."},{"name":"SpringHill Suites by Marriott St. Joseph Benton Harbor","source":"https://swmichigan.org/member/springhill-suites","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior"],"booking_route":"marriott.com (brand booking; not fetched)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":8,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":26,"blurb":"1255 Cinema Way, Benton Harbor, 269-338-8300, as listed by Visit Southwest Michigan: a \"Ninety-two-room all-suite property\" off Interstate 94, \"6 miles from both downtown St. Joseph and the Amtrak Station. Lake Michigan''s Silver Beach is 5.5 miles away\"; free hot breakfast, indoor pool. Marriott''s own page was not fetched."},{"name":"Hilton Garden Inn Benton Harbor/St. Joseph","source":"https://swmichigan.org/member/hilton-garden-inn-benton-harbor-st-joseph","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior"],"booking_route":"hilton.com (brand booking; not fetched)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":27,"blurb":"1300 Cinema Way, Benton Harbor, 269-926-5000, as listed by Visit Southwest Michigan: \"We''re off I-94, near golf courses and local breweries. Silver Beach on Lake Michigan''s shoreline is 15 minutes away\"; Garden Grille & Bar, indoor pool, pet friendly, \"ADA/ Wheelchair Accessible\", 106 guest rooms. Hilton''s own page was not fetched."},{"name":"Staybridge Suites Benton Harbor - St. Joseph","source":"https://swmichigan.org/member/staybridge-suites","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family"],"booking_route":"ihg.com (brand booking; not fetched)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":28,"blurb":"1275 Cinema Way, Benton Harbor, 269-371-0000, as listed by Visit Southwest Michigan: \"Spacious suites come with fully equipped kitchens\"; complimentary breakfast buffet, evening social three days a week, indoor pool, guest laundry. IHG''s own page was not fetched."},{"name":"The Inn at Harbor Shores","source":"https://swmichigan.org/member/inn-at-harbor-shores","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["golf","wellness","romance"],"booking_route":"own website (link on the Visit Southwest Michigan listing) or phone","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":29,"blurb":"800 Whitwam Drive, St. Joseph: \"Set along the scenic St. Joseph River and just moments from the beaches of Lake Michigan\"; Plank''s Tavern, a full-service spa, marina, indoor and outdoor pools, bike rentals, and the \"Jack Nicklaus Signature public golf course\". 269-983-1111."},{"name":"Hidden Ponds RV Resort - South Haven","source":"https://www.campspot.com/c/rv-camping-in-michigan/near-warren-dunes-state-park","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["motoring","senior"],"booking_route":"Campspot (campspot.com/park/hidden-ponds-rv-resort-south-haven-mi)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":3,"commission_pct_high":3,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":30,"blurb":"Campspot: 37 miles straight-line; \"spacious concrete pads with full hookups situated around peaceful, private fishing ponds\", a heated pool, wellness trails, pickleball and \"a dedicated off-leash dog park\"; starting at $79.00; 4.9 from 9 verified reviews."},{"name":"Riverfront Park Campground, Niles","source":"https://www.campspot.com/c/rv-camping-in-michigan/near-warren-dunes-state-park","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","motoring"],"booking_route":"Campspot (campspot.com/park/riverfront-park-campground-niles-mi)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":3,"commission_pct_high":3,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":31,"blurb":"Campspot: 18 miles straight-line; \"nestled in the woods along the scenic Dowagiac River\" with \"extra-large campsites, many with direct river or private pond frontage\"; general store, laundry, playground; no ratings yet."},{"name":"Silver Beach Hotel","source":"https://swmichigan.org/member/silver-beach-hotel","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["romance","family"],"booking_route":"own website (link on the Visit Southwest Michigan listing) or phone","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":32,"blurb":"100 Main Street, St. Joseph, 269-983-7341, as listed by Visit Southwest Michigan: \"90 minutes east of Chicago\", boutique streets and Lake Michigan beaches \"just a short walk away\"; \"All rooms have a balcony with a view!\""},{"name":"Staymaker at Journeyman Distillery","source":"https://www.journeyman.com/staymaker/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","culture"],"booking_route":"own website reservations or walk-in","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":33,"blurb":"Journeyman Distillery''s on-site restaurant in the Featherbone Factory, 109 Generations Drive, Three Oaks: \"Open 362 days a year\"; daily reservations or walk-ins; groups larger than 8 by email. (269) 820-2050."},{"name":"Redamak''s","source":"https://www.redamaks.com/faqs/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in only - no reservations","commission_status":"none","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":34,"blurb":"New Buffalo: \"The hamburger that made New Buffalo, Michigan famous!!\"; started by George and Gladys Redamak in 1946, Maroney-owned since July 15, 1975; opens for the season in \"Early March\" and closes for winter; \"No, we also don''t allow call ahead seating.\""},{"name":"Luisa''s Harbert Swedish Bakery & Market","source":"https://luisasswedishbakery.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in; online ordering","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":35,"blurb":"13698 Red Arrow Hwy, Harbert: \"The iconic Harbert Swedish Bakery has been providing Harbor Country with the best baked goods and prepared foods for over 100 years\"; open 8:00 am - 2:00 pm, Thursday - Sunday. 269.469.9037."},{"name":"Silver Beach Pizza","source":"https://silverbeachpizza.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family"],"booking_route":"own website reservations, carryout or delivery","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":36,"blurb":"410 Vine Street, St. Joseph: \"award-winning pizza and ice-cold schooners at Saint Joseph''s most iconic dining spot\" with Lake Michigan views; Mon-Thu 4-9pm, Fri 4-10pm, Sat 12-10pm, Sun 12-9pm. (269) 983-4743."},{"name":"Lake Michigan Shore Wine Trail","source":"https://miwinetrail.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["wine","culinary","romance"],"booking_route":"none needed - a trail of independent wineries","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":37,"blurb":"\"a collaboration of 15 quality focused wineries located in the Lake Michigan Shore AVA\"; \"Located at the 42nd parallel and the southern end of Lake Michigan, our region contains 90% of Michigan''s vineyards.\""},{"name":"Sarett Nature Center","source":"https://swmichigan.org/member/sarett-nature-center","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["wildlife","hiking","family"],"booking_route":"own website (link on the Visit Southwest Michigan listing)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":38,"blurb":"2300 N Benton Center Road, Benton Harbor, as listed by Visit Southwest Michigan: \"over 1,000 acres of protected land and eight miles of scenic trails\"; boardwalks over wetlands and fens; \"the tree top walkway\"; an electric-powered vehicle or balloon-tired wagon can be reserved for access. 269-927-4832."}],"faq":[{"q":"How much does it cost to get into Warren Dunes State Park?","a":"Vehicle entry needs a Michigan Recreation Passport. For non-Michigan-registered vehicles the DNR lists \"Annual $42\" and \"Daily $12 - good for entry and re-entry to any state park for the day.\" Michigan-registered vehicles pay \"$15 when purchased at time of license plate registration renewal\"; \"A daily pass for residents is not available.\"","source":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260828212031/https://www.michigan.gov/dnr/buy-and-apply/recreation-passport","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you camp at Warren Dunes State Park?","a":"Yes. The DNR lists the Mt. Randall Modern Campground (182 sites), the Hildebrandt Semi-Modern Campground (37 sites, \"no electrical service available\"), three Rustic Mini Cabins that each sleep six, and a Youth Group-Use Campground for groups up to 100. Reservations: \"800-447-2757 or reserve online\".","source":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260801110517/https://www.michigan.gov/recsearch/parks/WarrenDunes","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"How much is camping at Warren Dunes State Park?","a":"The DNR''s 2026 rates table lists Mount Randall at $60 (full hook-up), $50 (50-amp) and $45 (20/30-amp); Hildebrandt semi-modern at $40; the Mini Cabins at $80; and the rustic group camp at \"$20/group of 6\". The Recreation Passport is a separate fee.","source":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260522165156/https://www.michigan.gov/dnr/things-to-do/camping-and-lodging/camping-and-lodging-rates-and-operating-dates","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Does Warren Dunes State Park allow dogs?","a":"Yes, on part of the beach: \"Pets are allowed north of the northernmost swim buoy at the beach, providing 2.5 miles of shoreline open to pets. Pets must always be on a 6-foot leash and under an owner''s immediate control.\"","source":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260801110517/https://www.michigan.gov/recsearch/parks/WarrenDunes","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you swim at Warren Dunes State Park?","a":"\"A buoyed swim area is located along the day-use area on Lake Michigan.\" The DNR adds that buoys are \"typically in place from Memorial Day weekend through Labor Day\", that \"state parks do not have lifeguards\", and that under double red flags \"you''re not allowed to enter the water from the beach.\"","source":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260603183713/https://www.michigan.gov/dnr/education/safety-info/beach-safety","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you have alcohol at Warren Dunes State Park?","a":"Not in season: \"You may not possess or consume an alcoholic beverage in the park April 1 through Sept. 30 (unless the park manager has granted written authorization through an event permit).\"","source":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260801110517/https://www.michigan.gov/recsearch/parks/WarrenDunes","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Does Warren Dunes State Park have showers?","a":"The Mt. Randall Modern Campground has a toilet and shower building; Hildebrandt campers use \"three modern toilet and shower buildings ... at the Mt. Randall modern campground, just a five-minute walk away.\" On the beach, \"Each bathroom building offers two foot showers and bottle fillers.\"","source":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260801110517/https://www.michigan.gov/recsearch/parks/WarrenDunes","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you metal detect at Warren Dunes State Park?","a":"\"Metal detecting is allowed in certain park areas. Please consult the park map for designated locations and review applicable regulations. Only registered campers can metal detect in campgrounds.\"","source":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260801110517/https://www.michigan.gov/recsearch/parks/WarrenDunes","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"How many acres is Warren Dunes State Park?","a":"The DNR says the park \"provides 1,500 acres of recreational opportunities along the beautiful shore of Lake Michigan\", with \"3 miles of shoreline\" and dunes \"rising 260 feet above the lake.\" Visit Southwest Michigan gives a different figure, \"1,952 acres\".","source":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260801110517/https://www.michigan.gov/recsearch/parks/WarrenDunes","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"What time does Warren Dunes State Park open?","a":"Visit Southwest Michigan lists the hours as \"Year-round, Sunday-Saturday: 8 a.m. to 10 p.m.\"","source":"https://swmichigan.org/member/warren-dunes-state-park","accessed":"2026-10-03"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Warren Dunes State Park: Dunes, Beach & Camping | TravelWell","meta_description":"260-foot dunes, 3 miles of Lake Michigan shore, a dog beach, 182-site modern campground and mini cabins, plus nearby wineries, RV parks and hotels.","slug":"warren-dunes-state-park-michigan","primary_keyword":"Warren Dunes State Park","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination"},"hero":{"query":"Warren Dunes State Park Lake Michigan dunes"}}'::jsonb, 57),
  ('badlands-south-dakota', '12A', 'Badlands National Park', 'United States', 'Buttes, fossil beds and bison prairie', 'future', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'The Great Plains & Dakotas', '{"hiking","family","wildlife","culture","senior","parks"}', '{"dramatic","rugged","remote","wild"}', '{}', null, null, '{"safety":{"posture":"book-freely","source":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/usa","verified":"2026-10-08"},"jewels":[{"name":"Badlands Loop Road (Highway 240)","source":"https://www.nps.gov/thingstodo/badl-loop-road.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["family","senior","wildlife"],"booking_route":"none needed - park entrance fee only","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":1,"blurb":"a two-lane paved road through the North Unit, \"1-2 Hours\", with a dozen stops including Big Badlands, Yellow Mounds and Pinnacles overlooks; open year-round, 24/7; NPS: \"Do not stop in the road\" and \"the Loop Road does close due to weather conditions occasionally in the winter\""},{"name":"Notch Trail","source":"https://home.nps.gov/badl/planyourvisit/hiking-in-badlands.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["hiking","adventure"],"booking_route":"none needed","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":2,"blurb":"1.25 miles round trip, moderate to strenuous, 1.5-2 hours, through a canyon and up a ladder to a ledge view of the White River Valley; NPS: \"NOT recommended for anyone with a fear of heights. The trail can be treacherous during and after rains.\""},{"name":"Fossil Preparation Lab","source":"https://www.nps.gov/thingstodo/badl-ranger-programs.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["family","culture","senior"],"booking_route":"none needed - walk-in","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":3,"blurb":"\"The ONLY National Park where you can interact with paleontologists and interns\" as they prepare specimens; at Ben Reifel Visitor Center, 9:00 AM - 4:00 PM, May 23 - October 31, 2026, 20-60 minutes"},{"name":"Sage Creek Rim Road and Roberts Prairie Dog Town","source":"https://www.nps.gov/thingstodo/sage-creek-rim-road.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["wildlife","family","adventure"],"booking_route":"none needed","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":4,"blurb":"a 1-2 hour dirt/gravel drive (SD 590) where \"Bison, bighorn, prairie dogs and a wide variety of birds are frequently seen\", with four overlooks including Roberts Prairie Dog Town; \"may be temporarily closed during or after heavy rain or snow\"; NPS: keep \"a minimum of a 100-foot distance from any wildlife\""},{"name":"Door Trail","source":"https://home.nps.gov/badl/planyourvisit/hiking-in-badlands.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["family","senior","hiking"],"booking_route":"none needed","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":5,"blurb":"0.26 miles round trip, easy, about 20 minutes: an accessible boardwalk through \"the Door\", a break in the Badlands Wall, with marked posts continuing into the formations; site of the summer 8:30 am ranger Geology Walk"},{"name":"Window Trail","source":"https://home.nps.gov/badl/planyourvisit/hiking-in-badlands.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["senior","family"],"booking_route":"none needed","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":6,"blurb":"0.26 miles round trip, easy, about 20 minutes: a short accessible boardwalk to a natural window in the Badlands Wall looking into an eroded canyon"},{"name":"Ben Reifel Visitor Center","source":"https://www.nps.gov/thingstodo/visit-ben-reifel.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["family","senior","culture"],"booking_route":"none needed","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":7,"blurb":"the main visitor centre at Cedar Pass: museum exhibits \"from ancient mosasaurs to Lakota history\", the 25-minute film The Land of Stone and Light, a Badlands Natural History Association bookstore and Junior Ranger booklets; hours 7am-7pm summer, 8am-5pm spring and fall, 8am-4pm winter"},{"name":"Cedar Pass Lodge cabins","source":"https://staybadlands.com/stay/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["senior","family","romance"],"booking_route":"own website booking engine (staybadlands.com) or (855) 765-0737","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":8,"blurb":"in-park cabins (King, King Duplex, Double Queen, Double Queen & Futon, Double Queen Cottage, with ADA options), \"April 15th - October 15th\"; run by Explor Badlands LLC, \"a Concessioner under Contract with the U.S. Government\"; the lodge was founded by Ben Millard in 1926 as a dance hall, \"the first establishment in what would later become Badlands National Park\""},{"name":"Night Sky Program","source":"https://home.nps.gov/thingstodo/night-sky-badl.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["family","romance","senior"],"booking_route":"none needed","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":9,"blurb":"\"Park astronomers will guide you through the night sky\" at the Cedar Pass Campground Amphitheater, June - September (9:30 PM June-July, 9:00 PM August, 8:30 PM September), with telescopes; the NPS says \"visitors will be exposed to more than 7,500 stars\" on any given night"},{"name":"Castle Trail","source":"https://home.nps.gov/badl/planyourvisit/hiking-in-badlands.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["hiking","adventure"],"booking_route":"none needed","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":10,"blurb":"the park''s longest established trail, 10.2 miles round trip, moderate, about 5 hours, from the Door and Window parking area to the Fossil Exhibit Trail; can be split into shorter segments"},{"name":"Cedar Pass Campground","source":"https://www.recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/10288228","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["family","senior"],"booking_route":"recreation.gov reservation","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":11,"blurb":"96 sites in the Agate, Butte and Group loops near Ben Reifel Visitor Center and Cedar Pass Lodge, some with electric hookups; \"Quiet hours are from 10:00 pm - 6:00 am\"; campfires prohibited, portable propane grills permitted; phone (605) 433-5460"},{"name":"Wall Drug Store, Wall","source":"https://www.travelsouthdakota.com/city/wall","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["culinary","family","culture","group"],"booking_route":"walk-in (walldrug.com refused connection)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat","shop"],"draw_rank":12,"blurb":"\"Since 1931, Wall Drug has evolved into a 76,000-square-foot wonderland of free attractions, including the Western Art Gallery Restaurant\"; Travel South Dakota names the cafe''s \"legendary hot beef sandwiches with mashed potatoes and gravy, buffalo burgers\""},{"name":"Minuteman Missile National Historic Site","source":"https://www.nps.gov/mimi/planyourvisit/directions.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["culture","family","senior"],"booking_route":"advance reservation required for Delta-01 tours (route not confirmed - reservation page returned 404)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":13,"blurb":"three Cold War sites along 15 miles of I-90: the visitor center \"immediately north of I-90, exit 131\" (the park''s Interior exit), Launch Control Facility Delta-01 at Exit 127 and the Delta-09 silo at Exit 116; a 30-minute film; \"Advanced reservations are required for all guided-tours\" of Delta-01; phone 605-433-5552"},{"name":"Fossil Exhibit Trail","source":"https://home.nps.gov/badl/planyourvisit/hiking-in-badlands.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["family","senior","culture"],"booking_route":"none needed","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":14,"blurb":"0.34 miles round trip, easy: a \"Fully accessible boardwalk loop trail\" with \"fossil replicas and exhibits of now extinct creatures\"; ranger Fossil Talks at 10:30 am and 2:00 pm, May 17 - September 26, 2026"},{"name":"Water: one gallon per person per day (NPS kit)","source":"https://www.nps.gov/badl/planyourvisit/safety.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","expedition","family"],"booking_route":"affiliate retail referral (REI.com via AvantLink; Amazon Associates)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":3,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":15,"blurb":"The NPS safety page advises \"drinking 1 gallon of water per day\" and warns \"Summer in the badlands is hot and dry with temperatures often exceeding 100° Fahrenheit\"; for backcountry trips: \"Always carry at least one gallon of water per person per day\". The kit this asks for is water bottles or a hydration reservoir sized to a gallon a person."},{"name":"Sun and heat cover: SPF 15+, long sleeves, wide-brimmed hat (NPS kit)","source":"https://www.nps.gov/badl/planyourvisit/safety.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","family","senior"],"booking_route":"affiliate retail referral (REI.com via AvantLink; Amazon Associates apparel)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":4,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":16,"blurb":"The NPS advises \"wearing sunscreen with an SPF of 15 or higher, and covering up with long sleeves, pants, and a wide-brimmed hat\" and to \"dress in layers\"; summer heat \"often exceeding 100° Fahrenheit\"."},{"name":"Closed-toed boots for badlands terrain (NPS kit)","source":"https://www.nps.gov/badl/planyourvisit/safety.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","adventure","expedition"],"booking_route":"affiliate retail referral (REI.com via AvantLink; Amazon Associates shoes)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":4,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":17,"blurb":"The NPS: \"closed-toed shoes or boots are essential for hiking and exploring the badlands environment\"; \"Badlands terrain is unstable\", and prairie rattlesnakes \"seek shade under boardwalks, stairs, and tall grasses\" - \"Do not place your hands and feet in areas you cannot see\"."},{"name":"Sage Creek Campground","source":"https://www.nps.gov/badl/planyourvisit/eatingsleeping.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["expedition","wildlife","adventure"],"booking_route":"none - first-come, first-served, free","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":18,"blurb":"a free, first-come first-served campground of 22 sites off Sage Creek Rim Road; accessible vault toilets, rough terrain"},{"name":"Backcountry camping and open hiking (Sage Creek Wilderness, Deer Haven)","source":"https://www.nps.gov/thingstodo/backcountry-camping-badl.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["expedition","hiking","adventure","wildlife"],"booking_route":"none - free self-registration","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":19,"blurb":"\"an open hike park, meaning that you are free to hike and camp off-trail\"; no permit currently required but you must register at one of five points; camp \"at least 0.5 miles from a road or trail\"; \"Campfires are not allowed under any circumstances\"; \"Always carry at least one gallon of water per person per day\"; backcountry camping is currently prohibited in the South Unit"},{"name":"Badlands-White River KOA, Interior","source":"https://maps.campendium.com/us/interior-sd/camping-rv/badlands-white-river-koa","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","glamping","motoring"],"booking_route":"koa.com or (605) 433-5337 (koa.com not fetched - HTTP 403)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":20,"blurb":"80 sites at 20720 SD Highway 44, Interior: Deluxe Cabins, Camping Cabins, tepees, tent sites and full-hookup RV sites (30/50 amp, water, sewer; max length \"60ft\"), with a pool, mini golf, playground, laundry and dump stations; season \"April - Oct.\"; (605) 433-5337. koa.com returned 403, so this rests on Campendium."},{"name":"Waysides restaurant, Cedar Pass","source":"https://staybadlands.com/dine/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["culinary","family","culture"],"booking_route":"walk-in - no reservations required","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":21,"blurb":"\"The only location to purchase food in Badlands National Park\" (NPS); Great Plains specialties with bison, blue corn, wild rice, chokecherries; 7:00 am - 8:00 pm, no reservations required; Travel South Dakota lists the Cedar Pass restaurant''s \"Sioux Indian Taco\""},{"name":"Sheep Mountain Table","source":"https://www.nps.gov/thingstodo/sheep-mtn-table.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["adventure","hiking"],"booking_route":"none needed","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":22,"blurb":"a 5-mile dirt road to an overlook on the North/South Unit border, plus 2.5 miles more for high-clearance vehicles only; four-wheel drive recommended; NPS: \"should not be driven during or after storms\"; call (605) 433-5361 for status"},{"name":"White River Visitor Center (South Unit)","source":"https://www.nps.gov/thingstodo/white-river-vc.htm","accessed":"