during and after rains and can be dangerous during extreme heat.\""},{"name":"Medicine Root Loop Trail","source":"https://home.nps.gov/badl/planyourvisit/hiking-in-badlands.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["hiking","wildlife"],"booking_route":"none needed","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":27,"blurb":"4.18 miles round trip, moderate, about 2 hours, through mixed-grass prairie with distant Badlands views; reached from the Old Northeast Road pulloff or the Castle and Saddle Pass trails"},{"name":"Badlands Astronomy Festival","source":"https://www.nps.gov/thingstodo/badl-astronomy-festival.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["family","culture"],"booking_route":"none needed - schedule at Ben Reifel Visitor Center","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":28,"blurb":"a three-day festival (July 17-19, 2026) with a scale-model solar system walk, solar observing, speakers on topics including Lakota astronomy, and evening telescopes; \"events do not require advance registration or tickets\"; Minuteman Missile NHS runs paper rocket-building"},{"name":"Summer ranger programmes","source":"https://www.nps.gov/thingstodo/badl-ranger-programs.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["family","senior","hiking","wildlife"],"booking_route":"none needed","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":29,"blurb":"Geology Walk on the Door Trail (8:30 AM), Prairie Walk from Ben Reifel (5:30-6:30 PM, \"easy to moderate prairie hike\" off-trail) and the Evening Program at the Cedar Pass Amphitheater on topics including \"bison, bighorn sheep, fossils\"; May 17 - September 26, 2026"},{"name":"Junior Ranger and I Walked the Badlands","source":"https://www.nps.gov/badl/learn/kidsyouth/index.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["family"],"booking_route":"none needed","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":30,"blurb":"\"Pick up a Junior Ranger Booklet at the visitor center and turn it in to earn a Junior Ranger badge\"; a GPS Adventure earns an \"I Walked the Badlands\" patch; an online Pick Your Park Adventure earns a patch by mail"},{"name":"Badlands Hotel & Campground, Interior","source":"https://badlandshotelandcampground.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["family","group"],"booking_route":"own website booking; 605-433-5335; also listed on Hipcamp","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":31,"blurb":"rooms, a 2-bedroom apartment, 30/50-amp RV sites including pull-throughs, standard and group tent sites (up to 30), fire pits, laundry and two bathhouses at 900 SD Hwy 377; \"Located just a mile from the iconic Badlands National Park\""},{"name":"Circle View Guest Ranch, Interior","source":"https://www.circleviewranch.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["culture","romance","senior","family"],"booking_route":"own website availability system; 605-433-5582","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":32,"blurb":"a working cattle ranch on 2,800 acres with \"badlands formations, a river valley\", seven guestrooms with private baths and a full ranch breakfast at 7:30am in the Kruse family kitchen; open year-round; 20055 E. Highway 44"},{"name":"Badlands Frontier Cabins, Wall","source":"https://www.frontiercabins.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["family","senior","group"],"booking_route":"online via resontheweb.com; 605-279-2619","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":33,"blurb":"\"Thirty-Three (33) authentic custom built log cabins with modern amenities\", private baths and daily housekeeping at 1101 Glenn Street, \"just six miles from the entrance to Badlands National Park\""},{"name":"Fly Badlands scenic flights, Wall","so