ance"],"booking_route":"not observed","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":43,"blurb":"per Travel South Dakota, \"Specializing in locally raised meat\" - farm-to-table beef, lamb and pork - with \"generous portions and decadent desserts\""},{"name":"Salty Steer, Wall","source":"https://www.travelsouthdakota.com/restaurants/near-the-badlands","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["culinary","group"],"booking_route":"not observed","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":44,"blurb":"per Travel South Dakota, \"burgers, steaks, pasta and local craft beer, with an emphasis on fresh, locally sourced ingredients\""},{"name":"Badlands Saloon & Grille, Wall","source":"https://www.travelsouthdakota.com/restaurants/near-the-badlands","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["culinary","group"],"booking_route":"not observed","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":45,"blurb":"per Travel South Dakota, \"hearty burgers, steaks and pizza\" with a focus on \"fresh ingredients and family recipes\""},{"name":"Cowboy Corner, Interior","source":"https://www.travelsouthdakota.com/restaurants/near-the-badlands","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["culinary","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat","shop"],"draw_rank":46,"blurb":"per Travel South Dakota, a \"convenience store with a café that serves lunch and occasionally dinner on weekends\""},{"name":"Wagon Wheel Bar & Grill, Interior","source":"https://www.travelsouthdakota.com/restaurants/near-the-badlands","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["culinary","group"],"booking_route":"walk-in","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":47,"blurb":"per Travel South Dakota, a bar \"serving some food, including pizza and burgers\" with \"a full bar with whiskey, beer, and pop\""},{"name":"Wakin'' Bacon food truck, Wall","source":"https://www.travelsouthdakota.com/city/wall","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["culinary"],"booking_route":"walk-in","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":48,"blurb":"per Travel South Dakota, a seasonal food truck (April-October) offering food, beer and retail items"},{"name":"National Grasslands Visitor Center, Wall","source":"https://www.travelsouthdakota.com/city/wall","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["culture","wildlife","senior"],"booking_route":"not observed (fs.usda.gov returned 403)","commission_status":"unknown","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":49,"blurb":"per Travel South Dakota, \"the only visitor center dedicated to interpreting the entire network of 20 national grasslands managed by the U.S. Forest Service\""},{"name":"Bigfoot Pass picnic area","source":"https://www.nps.gov/badl/planyourvisit/accessibility.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["senior","family"],"booking_route":"none needed","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":50,"blurb":"an accessible picnic stop with \"reserved parking, ramps, and an accessible vault toilet\""},{"name":"Dahl''s Chainsaw Art, Wall area","source":"https://www.travelsouthdakota.com/city/wall","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["culture","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["shop","activities"],"draw_rank":51,"blurb":"per Travel South Dakota, \"Watch live chainsaw carving at [this] roadside studio\" of wood sculptures"}],"faq":[{"q":"What is the Badlands National Park entrance fee?","a":"The NPS lists $30 for a private vehicle, $25 for a motorcycle and $15 for an individual on foot or bicycle, each valid for 7 days, and $55 for a Badlands annual pass. \"Entrance fees are collected year round.\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/badl/planyourvisit/fees.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"Is Badlands National Park open 24 hours?","a":"Yes. The NPS states \"Badlands National Park is open 24 hours a day, seven days a week\", though winter weather may temporarily close roads.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/badl/planyourvisit/hours.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"Can you camp in Badlands National Park?","a":"Yes. The NPS lists Cedar Pass Campground (96 sites, some with electric hookups, reserved on recreation.gov) and Sage Creek Campground, \"free, first-come first-serve, 22 sites\".","source":"https://www.nps.gov/badl/planyourvisit/eatingsleeping.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"Do you need a permit for Badlands National Park?","a":"Not for backcountry camping at present. The NPS says \"No permits are currently required for overnight stays\", but you must register at one of five locations, camp \"at least 0.5 miles from a road or trail\", and \"Campfires are not allowed under any circumstances\". Backcountry camping is currently prohibited in the South Unit.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/thingstodo/backcountry-camping-badl.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"Where can you see wildlife in Badlands National Park?","a":"The NPS says \"Bison, bighorn, prairie dogs and a wide variety of birds are frequently seen from Sage Creek Rim Road\", a gravel road that may close after heavy rain or snow. Keep \"a minimum of a 100-foot distance from any wildlife\".","source":"https://www.nps.gov/thingstodo/sage-creek-rim-road.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"What can you do at Badlands National Park with kids?","a":"The Fossil Preparation Lab at Ben Reifel Visitor Center is open 9:00 AM - 4:00 PM, May 23 - October 31, 2026; the NPS calls Badlands \"The ONLY National Park where you can interact with paleontologists and interns\". Summer ranger programmes include Fossil Talks and an evening Night Sky Program.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/thingstodo/badl-ranger-programs.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"Where can you eat in Badlands National Park?","a":"The NPS says the only place to buy food in the park is Cedar Pass Lodge, near Ben Reifel Visitor Center; its restaurant is Waysides.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/badl/planyourvisit/eatingsleeping.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"How far is Badlands National Park from Rapid City?","a":"\"Badlands National Park is located 75 miles east of Rapid City, South Dakota\", with entrances from I-90 at Exit 131 (Interior) and Exit 110 (Wall).","source":"https://www.nps.gov/badl/planyourvisit/directions.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"What should you wear to Badlands National Park?","a":"The NPS advises \"wearing sunscreen with an SPF of 15 or higher, and covering up with long sleeves, pants, and a wide-brimmed hat\", to \"dress in layers\", and says \"closed-toed shoes or boots are essential for hiking and exploring the badlands environment\". It also advises \"drinking 1 gallon of water per day\".","source":"https://www.nps.gov/badl/planyourvisit/safety.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"What is the weather like in Badlands National Park in October?","a":"The NPS gives \"October Averages: High 68°F, Low 39°F, Precipitation 0.90 inches\" and says in fall \"Weather becomes more stable\".","source":"https://www.nps.gov/badl/planyourvisit/weather.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Badlands National Park: Loop Road, Fossil Lab, Bison & Where to Stay | TravelWell","meta_description":"Badlands National Park, South Dakota: the Loop Road and Notch Trail, the fossil lab, bison on Sage Creek Rim Road, fees, and stays from Cedar Pass to Wall.","slug":"badlands-national-park-south-dakota","primary_keyword":"Badlands National Park","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination"},"hero":{"query":"Badlands National Park, South Dakota"}}'::jsonb, 58)
